COLLDATA("tadabburen","en",[[165,"§Al-A'raf\ndeeds\nRepeat this supplication, and ask Allah to free the Muslims held in captive.\nShare a message in which you show that the risk of bad advisors to those in authority is far worse than that to others.\nSend a message to an afflicted person, in which you urge him to be patient and steadfast, and give him good tidings of reward and a good outcome.\nguid\nOne of the most dangerous types of lying to society is the lying of its leaders.\nThe bad advisors to those who are in power is evil for the country and the people.\nWorship and righteousness are conditions for inheriting the earth.\nrefl\nإِنَّ هَٰذَا لَمَكۡرٞ مَّكَرۡتُمُوهُ فِي ٱلۡمَدِينَةِ\nMoses (peace be upon him) neither knew any of them nor saw or met them before. Pharaoh knew that, but he claimed otherwise to deceive the ignorant masses of his kingdom, as Allah says, (Thus he made a fool of his people and they obeyed him) [43:54]. Certainly, a people who believed Pharaoh in his statement, (I am your lord, the most high) [79:24], are among the most ignorant and misguided creatures of Allah. Ibn Kathir: 2/228.\nWhat did Pharaoh mean when he said: (Indeed, this is a conspiracy which you conspired in the city)?\nقَالُوٓاْ إِنَّآ إِلَىٰ رَبِّنَا مُنقَلِبُونَ ١٢٥\nCertainly, Allah's punishment is more severe than your punishment, and His torment for what you are calling us to, this day, and the magic you forced us to practice, is greater than your torment. Therefore, we will observe patience in the face of your punishment today, so that we are saved from Allah's torment. Ibn Kathir: 2/228.\nWhat is the comparison the magicians made that helped them remain steadfast in faith?\nوَمَا تَنقِمُ مِنَّآ إِلَّآ أَنۡ ءَامَنَّا بِـَٔايَٰتِ رَبِّنَا لَمَّا جَآءَتۡنَاۚ\nAta’ (a prominent scholar) said: It means that we have made no assumed sin deserving your punishment except that (we believed in the signs of our Lord). Al-Baghawi: 2/138.\nWhat is the assumed sin for which the tyrants have enmity toward the believers?\nرَبَّنَآ أَفۡرِغۡ عَلَيۡنَا صَبۡرٗا\nMeaning: Great patience, as is indicated by use of the indefinite form in the original Arabic text. This was a great trial that would lead to loss of life, for which a great deal of patience is required to remain steadfast and confident in faith, and to dispel panic. Al-Saadi: 300.\nAfter they believed in Allah, why did the magicians ask Him to pour patience upon them?\nرَبَّنَآ أَفۡرِغۡ عَلَيۡنَا صَبۡرٗا وَتَوَفَّنَا مُسۡلِمِينَ ١٢٦\nMeaning: Give us the strength to endure what Pharaoh threatened us with; since this type of threat was unbearable to humans, they asked Allah to give them extraordinary patience, similar to pouring and emptying a container of patience. They asked to die in submission to Allah (Islam), indicating that they have no desire for life, and were indifferent to Pharaoh's threat. Their only hope was to be saved in the Hereafter, and attain Allah's reward, which defeated Pharaoh and rendered his threat in vain. Ibn Ashur: 9/56.\nWhen faith enters the heart, the Hereafter becomes more important than this worldly life. Explain in the light of this verse.\nقَالَ عَسَىٰ رَبُّكُمۡ أَن يُهۡلِكَ عَدُوَّكُمۡ وَيَسۡتَخۡلِفَكُمۡ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ فَيَنظُرَ كَيۡفَ تَعۡمَلُونَ ١٢٩\n(It may be), is an expression of hope rather than assertion to show respect toward Allah, to eliminate their dependance on their actions so that they increase their share of righteousness and to be worthy of Allah's pleasure and help. Ibn Ashur: 9/62.\nWhy did Moses (peace be upon him) use an expression of hope (It may be), rather than assertion in this verse?\nوَلَقَدۡ أَخَذۡنَآ ءَالَ فِرۡعَوۡنَ بِٱلسِّنِينَ وَنَقۡصٖ مِّنَ ٱلثَّمَرَٰتِ لَعَلَّهُمۡ يَذَّكَّرُونَ ١٣٠\n(With years), it means drought and aridness of the land. In Arabic, the word (year) refers to the drought. (And a deficiency in fruits), the fruits were ruined by pests and defects. Qatadah said: \"The drought was for the nomads, and the deficiency in fruits was for the people of the cities.\" (That perhaps they would be reminded), that they may become admonished, as hardship softens the hearts and endears Allah's blessings to them. Al-Baghawi: 2/139.\nWhat is the wisdom behind seizing people with hardships and trials?\nwords\nمُنقَلِبُونَWe will return\nأَفرِغPour on us\nبِالسِّنِينَWith years of famine"],[166,"§Al-A'raf\ndeeds\nShare a message or deliver a speech in which you warn others against having enmity toward the allies of Allah and their religion, as their supplications are accepted by Allah.\nRecall three instances where Allah has given victory to the oppressed and weak believers over their strong enemy.\nIdentify three misfortunes that occurred in society due to flaunting of sins, and not enjoining what is good or forbidding what is evil.\nguid\nOne must thank Allah for His blessings, knowing that he has no credit for it, but rather it is Allah's pure grace.\nDefiance and stubbornness can greatly harm oneself.\nBeware of being heedless of Allah's signs, for it is a reason for punishment and torment.\nrefl\nفَإِذَا جَآءَتۡهُمُ ٱلۡحَسَنَةُ قَالُواْ لَنَا هَٰذِهِۦۖ\nMeaning: We deserve it; however, they did not give thanks to Allah for it. Al-Saadi: 301.\nWhat is the stance of the disbelievers on the blessings of Allah?\nفَإِذَا جَآءَتۡهُمُ ٱلۡحَسَنَةُ قَالُواْ لَنَا هَٰذِهِۦۖ وَإِن تُصِبۡهُمۡ سَيِّئَةٞ يَطَّيَّرُواْ بِمُوسَىٰ وَمَن مَّعَهُۥٓۗ أَلَآ إِنَّمَا طَٰٓئِرُهُمۡ عِندَ ٱللَّهِ وَلَٰكِنَّ أَكۡثَرَهُمۡ لَا يَعۡلَمُونَ ١٣١\n(But most of them do not know) that the drought and hardships which afflicted them were decreed by Allah for their sins. Al-Qurtubi: 9/308.\nDo most people know the reason for punishments and tribulations which afflict them?\nفَأَرۡسَلۡنَا عَلَيۡهِمُ ٱلطُّوفَانَ وَٱلۡجَرَادَ وَٱلۡقُمَّلَ وَٱلضَّفَادِعَ وَٱلدَّمَ ءَايَٰتٖ مُّفَصَّلَٰتٖ فَٱسۡتَكۡبَرُواْ وَكَانُواْ قَوۡمٗا مُّجۡرِمِينَ ١٣٣\nAllah calls these tribulations (signs) since they were proofs of the truthfulness of Moses (peace be upon him), as they presented a challenge and were indications of Allah's wrath upon them. Ibn Ashur: 9/70.\nIn this verse, Allah calls these tribulations (signs), why?\nفَٱنتَقَمۡنَا مِنۡهُمۡ فَأَغۡرَقۡنَٰهُمۡ فِي ٱلۡيَمِّ بِأَنَّهُمۡ كَذَّبُواْ بِـَٔايَٰتِنَا وَكَانُواْ عَنۡهَا غَٰفِلِينَ ١٣٦\n(And were heedless of them) they did not learn from these signs, so they became heedless of them. Al-Qurtubi: 9/315.\nWhat is the reality of heedlessness?\nفَٱنتَقَمۡنَا مِنۡهُمۡ فَأَغۡرَقۡنَٰهُمۡ فِي ٱلۡيَمِّ بِأَنَّهُمۡ كَذَّبُواْ بِـَٔايَٰتِنَا وَكَانُواْ عَنۡهَا غَٰفِلِينَ ١٣٦\nMeaning: We drowned them as a recompense for their rejection of the signs. Heedlessness is the distraction of the mind from remembering things, which meant, in this case, intentional heedlessness, turning away from reflecting on the signs, and refusing to see them as evidence of the truthfulness of Moses (peace be upon him). Ibn Ashur: 9/75.\nWhat type of heedlessness did the people of Pharaoh experience?\nوَأَوۡرَثۡنَا ٱلۡقَوۡمَ ٱلَّذِينَ كَانُواْ يُسۡتَضۡعَفُونَ مَشَٰرِقَ ٱلۡأَرۡضِ وَمَغَٰرِبَهَا ٱلَّتِي بَٰرَكۡنَا فِيهَاۖ\nAllah mentions that He blessed the land of the Levant (Ash-Sham, which is presently the region of Syria, Lebanon, Jordan and Palestine) in many verses of the Quran, such as (And We made the people who had been oppressed to inherit the lands of the east and west that We had blessed). Ibn Taimyah: 3/194.\nThis verse proves that the land of the Levant is blessed. Explain.\nوَتَمَّتۡ كَلِمَتُ رَبِّكَ ٱلۡحُسۡنَىٰ عَلَىٰ بَنِيٓ إِسۡرَٰٓءِيلَ بِمَا صَبَرُواْۖ\nMeaning: The fulfillment of Allah's good word is the realization of His promise to them of achieving victory over Pharaoh and his demise. Ibn Taimyah: 3/194.\nWhat is the meaning of fulfillment of Allah's good word in this verse?\nwords\nيَطَّيَّرُواThey saw an evil omen\nطَائِرُهُم عِندَ اللَّهِTheir misfortune [drought] is decreed by Allah\nوَالقُمَّلَInsects that destroyed their crops and animals"],[167,"§Al-A'raf\ndeeds\nGive a speech or share a message about the risk of polytheism (shirk) and its effect in invalidating good deeds.\nUse a wise method to educate those who fall into a type of shirk, and direct them to the truth.\nSay, \"Glorified is Allah and praised is He, Glorified is Allah the Great.\" a hundred times.\nguid\nThe worst type of ignorance is the ignorance of Tawhīd (monotheism).\nKeeping appointments is something that is liked and encouraged in Sharia, and it is one of the traits of truthful people.\nRighteousness is a path of Prophets, so follow their path, and do not follow the path of those who spread corruption.\nrefl\nوَجَٰوَزۡنَا بِبَنِيٓ إِسۡرَٰٓءِيلَ ٱلۡبَحۡرَ فَأَتَوۡاْ عَلَىٰ قَوۡمٖ يَعۡكُفُونَ عَلَىٰٓ أَصۡنَامٖ لَّهُمۡۚ قَالُواْ يَٰمُوسَى ٱجۡعَل لَّنَآ إِلَٰهٗا كَمَا لَهُمۡ ءَالِهَةٞۚ قَالَ إِنَّكُمۡ قَوۡمٞ تَجۡهَلُونَ ١٣٨\n(He said, \"You are indeed an ignorant people\"), what ignorance could be greater than that of one who is ignorant of his Lord and Creator, and wants to make others equal to Him, which they do not possess any power to bring benefit or cause harm, to cause death or bring life or bring about resurrection. Al-Saadi: 302.\nWhat is the worst kind of ignorance? Why?\nقَالُواْ يَٰمُوسَى ٱجۡعَل لَّنَآ إِلَٰهٗا كَمَا لَهُمۡ ءَالِهَةٞۚ قَالَ إِنَّكُمۡ قَوۡمٞ تَجۡهَلُونَ ١٣٨\nMoses' (peace be upon him) description of them as (ignorant people) is confirmed by the use of the noun clause (in Arabic) which indicates that \"ignorance\" is a fixed trait of them and is rooted in their souls. Otherwise, they would, essentially, have had a deterrence from asking such a question. Ibn Ashur: 9/82.\nThis verse indicates that ignorance may lead to shirk. How?\nقَالَ أَغَيۡرَ ٱللَّهِ أَبۡغِيكُمۡ إِلَٰهٗا وَهُوَ فَضَّلَكُمۡ عَلَى ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ١٤٠\n(He has favored you above the worlds) means: Allah favored them above the nations of their times for many reasons: First: They were descendants of Messengers and Prophets. Second: The Messengers and Prophets came from among them. Third: Allah has guided them to His Oneness, and saved them from the religion of Pharaoh after they floundered in it. Fourth: Allah has freed them from bondage, made them the owners of a blessed land, and helped them with His victory and signs. Fifth: Allah has sent to them a Messenger to rule them with Sharia. All of these favors were not given to a nation of their times except them. Ibn Ashur: 9/84.\nWhat is meant by (above the worlds)? What were the things for which Allah favored the Children of Israel above the worlds?\nوَقَالَ مُوسَىٰ لِأَخِيهِ هَٰرُونَ ٱخۡلُفۡنِي فِي قَوۡمِي وَأَصۡلِحۡ وَلَا تَتَّبِعۡ سَبِيلَ ٱلۡمُفۡسِدِينَ ١٤٢\nWhen Moses (peace be upon him) went to the place appointed by his Lord, at the time appointed, he said to Aaron (peace be upon him), leaving him in charge of the Israelites because of his concern and kindness toward them: (Take my place among my people in my absence), which means: Be my deputy among them and deal with them as I have been dealing with them (keep things right) follow the path that maintains order and peace (and do not follow the way of those who spread corruption) namely, those who commit sins. Al-Saadi: 302.\nThe Prophets (peace be upon them), among all people, had more compassion and concern for their people. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَقَالَ مُوسَىٰ لِأَخِيهِ هَٰرُونَ ٱخۡلُفۡنِي فِي قَوۡمِي وَأَصۡلِحۡ وَلَا تَتَّبِعۡ سَبِيلَ ٱلۡمُفۡسِدِينَ ١٤٢\nMoses (peace be upon him) left his brother Aaron (peace be upon him) with the Children of Israel, and commanded him to use wisdom and refrain from mischief. This was only a reminder, for Aaron (peace be upon him) was an honorable and noble Prophet who had grace and an exalted standard with Allah. Ibn Kathir: 2/234.\nAll righteous people need reminding, even the Prophets (peace be upon them). Explain.\nوَلَٰكِنِ ٱنظُرۡ إِلَى ٱلۡجَبَلِ فَإِنِ ٱسۡتَقَرَّ مَكَانَهُۥ فَسَوۡفَ تَرَىٰنِيۚ فَلَمَّا تَجَلَّىٰ رَبُّهُۥ لِلۡجَبَلِ جَعَلَهُۥ دَكّٗا وَخَرَّ مُوسَىٰ صَعِقٗاۚ\nMeaning: The mountain is bigger and more solid than you; (When his Lord appeared to the mountain), and when Moses saw the mountain crumbling and turning to dust, he fell unconscious. Ibn Kathir: 2/235.\nThis verse describes an aspect of the greatness of Allah. Explain.\nفَلَمَّآ أَفَاقَ قَالَ سُبۡحَٰنَكَ تُبۡتُ إِلَيۡكَ وَأَنَا۠ أَوَّلُ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ ١٤٣\nMoses (peace be upon him) said that by virtue of turning in repentance to Allah with humbleness when he witnessed the signs. There is a consensus among Muslims that this repentance was not for a committed sin since all Prophets were infallible. Al-Qurtubi: 10/439.\nDoes seeking Allah's forgiveness occur only for a sin?\nwords\nوَجَاوَزنَاAnd we led [them across the sea]\nيَعكُفُونَThey intent in devotion to worship\nإِلَهًاAn idol\nمُتَبَّرٌDoomed to destruction\nيَسُومُونَكُمThey were afflicting you\nلِمِيقَاتِنَاTo Our appointed time\nصَعِقًاHe fell unconscious"],[168,"§Al-A'raf\ndeeds\nAdopt a new approach, today, that helps you take the Quran more diligently such as striving to act by what you recite and thanking Allah for making you love the Quran.\nRemind yourself of five blessings that Allah bestowed upon you and thank Him for them.\nSeek refuge with Allah from turning your heart away from His remembrance and from comprehending the Quran.\nguid\nArrogance is one of the biggest factors that turn people away from comprehending the verses of Allah.\nThis verse sharply rebukes stupidity, stagnation, and man's lack of thinking about his condition, reality and what is around him.\nWhen Allah decrees goodness for His servant, He inspires him to repent after committing a sin, so, he regrets it and asks for forgiveness.\nrefl\nقَالَ يَٰمُوسَىٰٓ إِنِّي ٱصۡطَفَيۡتُكَ عَلَى ٱلنَّاسِ\nAllah states that He spoke to Moses directly and informed him that He had chosen him above the people of his time with His Message and His words. Here, we should mention that there is no doubt that Muhammad (ﷺ) is the chief of all the Children of Adam, the former and later among them. This is why Allah has chosen him to be the final and last Prophet and Messenger, whose Sharia shall remain dominant and valid until the commencement of the Last Hour, and his followers exceed in number the followers of all Prophets and Messengers. Ibn Kathir: 2/236.\nDoes this verse indicate the preference of Moses over our Prophet (peace be upon them)?\nقَالَ يَٰمُوسَىٰٓ إِنِّي ٱصۡطَفَيۡتُكَ عَلَى ٱلنَّاسِ بِرِسَٰلَٰتِي وَبِكَلَٰمِي\nWhen Allah did not allow him to see Him -after he had longed for that- He bestowed much good upon him. Al-Saadi: 302.\nIf Allah withholds a good thing from a true believer, He gives him something better instead. How can you infer this rule from the above verse?\nفَخُذۡهَا بِقُوَّةٖ وَأۡمُرۡ قَوۡمَكَ يَأۡخُذُواْ بِأَحۡسَنِهَاۚ سَأُوْرِيكُمۡ دَارَ ٱلۡفَٰسِقِينَ ١٤٥\n(Take them with determination), take it with earnestness and diligence. It is also said that it means: Take it with strength of heart and good resolve, because if it is taken with weak intention, it will lead to slackness. Al-Baghawi: 2/152.\nHow should we take the revelation of Allah as commanded by Him?\nفَخُذۡهَا بِقُوَّةٖ وَأۡمُرۡ قَوۡمَكَ يَأۡخُذُواْ بِأَحۡسَنِهَاۚ سَأُوْرِيكُمۡ دَارَ ٱلۡفَٰسِقِينَ ١٤٥\nThis verse indicates that from among the revelations, there is good and there is best. Ibn Taimyah: 3/198.\nBecoming closer to Allah by following His revelation can be at different levels. Explain in the light of this verse.\nسَأَصۡرِفُ عَنۡ ءَايَٰتِيَ ٱلَّذِينَ يَتَكَبَّرُونَ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ بِغَيۡرِ ٱلۡحَقِّ وَإِن يَرَوۡاْ كُلَّ ءَايَةٖ لَّا يُؤۡمِنُواْ بِهَا وَإِن يَرَوۡاْ سَبِيلَ ٱلرُّشۡدِ لَا يَتَّخِذُوهُ سَبِيلٗا وَإِن يَرَوۡاْ سَبِيلَ ٱلۡغَيِّ يَتَّخِذُوهُ سَبِيلٗاۚ\nIbn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him)said: \"[Allah says]: I will turn away from My signs those who deal with My servants arrogantly, and fight My allies, so that they will not believe in Me.\" This means: I will turn them away from accepting and believing My signs. They were punished by being precluded from guidance, as Allah says, (And when they deviated, Allah caused their hearts to deviate)[61:5]. Al-Baghawi: 2/152.\nWhat are the severest punishment for arrogant people?\nسَأَصۡرِفُ عَنۡ ءَايَٰتِيَ ٱلَّذِينَ يَتَكَبَّرُونَ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ بِغَيۡرِ ٱلۡحَقِّ\nOne of the righteous predecessors said: \"Knowledge cannot be attained by a shy person or an arrogant one.\" Another said: \"Whoever does not endure the humility to learn for an hour, will remain humiliated by his ignorance forever.\" Ibn Kathir: 2/237.\nThis verse states some guidelines for a student who seeks knowledge. What are they?\nسَأَصۡرِفُ عَنۡ ءَايَٰتِيَ ٱلَّذِينَ يَتَكَبَّرُونَ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ بِغَيۡرِ ٱلۡحَقِّ\nSince a copy of the Quran can only be touched after purifying the body, also the Quranic meanings can only be perceived by the pure hearts whereas impure hearts will not grasp its truths. This is a valid meaning, as Allah says, (I will turn away from My signs those who are arrogant in the land without any right). One of the righteous predecessors said: \"[Allah says], I will prevent their hearts from comprehending the Quran.\" Ibn Taimyah: 3/198.\nThe risk of arrogance is that it prevents from comprehending the Quran. Explain\nwords\nالأَلوَاحِTablets of the Torah\nحَبِطَتBecame worthless\nحُلِيِّهِمTheir golden jewelry\nخُوَارٌA lowing sound\nسُقِطَ فِي أَيدِيهِمThey regretted"],[169,"§Al-A'raf\ndeeds\nIf you come across something that makes you angry today, perform ablution, sit down if you are standing, and seek refuge with Allah from satan, the accursed.\nAsk for Allah's forgiveness, and repent to Him for the mistakes and misdeeds that you have committed.\nPray and humble yourself to Allah not to punish us for what the foolish among us did.\nguid\nA brother has the right to admonish his Muslim brother, but at a distance from the ears of those who await a misfortune to befall Islam to rejoice over it.\nA person of religious innovation and shirk is covered by humiliation, even if he pretends to be proud of his status or wealth.\nNeglecting to enjoin good and forbid evil leads to the destruction and downfall of society.\nrefl\nوَلَمَّا رَجَعَ مُوسَىٰٓ إِلَىٰ قَوۡمِهِۦ غَضۡبَٰنَ أَسِفٗا قَالَ بِئۡسَمَا خَلَفۡتُمُونِي مِنۢ بَعۡدِيٓۖ\nMoses (peace be upon him) was filled with anger and rage toward them, because he cared so much for them and was sincere and compassionate toward them. Al-Saadi: 303.\nWhat was the reason for the fury and grief of Moses (u)?\nأَعَجِلۡتُمۡ أَمۡرَ رَبِّكُمۡۖ\nHaste is actioning something before its right time, which is censured. Meanwhile, quickness is performing something at its earliest time, which is praised. Al-Qurtubi: 9/338.\nWhat is the difference between haste and quickness? Which one is praised?\nقَالَ ٱبۡنَ أُمَّ إِنَّ ٱلۡقَوۡمَ ٱسۡتَضۡعَفُونِي وَكَادُواْ يَقۡتُلُونَنِي\nAaron (u) said, (O son of my mother), so that Moses (u) would have more compassion and leniency toward him, even though Aaron was also the son of Moses' father.Ibn Kathir: 2/238.\nThe righteous choose the best words to attain the intended result. Explain in the light of this verse.\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱتَّخَذُواْ ٱلۡعِجۡلَ سَيَنَالُهُمۡ غَضَبٞ مِّن رَّبِّهِمۡ وَذِلَّةٞ فِي ٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنۡيَاۚ وَكَذَٰلِكَ نَجۡزِي ٱلۡمُفۡتَرِينَ ١٥٢\nThe consequence of their abhorred action was the disgrace and humiliation that they suffered in the life of this world. Allah says, (This is how We recompense those who invent falsehood), this incudes all those who invent a religious innovation. Surely, the disgrace resulting from inventing a religious innovation and defying Allah's guidance will be placed in the heart and from there on to the shoulders. Al-Hasan Al-Basri said: \"The disgrace of religious innovation will weigh on their shoulders even if they were to gallop on their mules or trot on their work horses.\" Sufyan bin Uyaynah said: \"Every person who invents a religious innovation will be disgraced.\" Ibn Kathir: 2/238.\nWhat is the consequence of inventing a religious innovation?\nوَلَمَّا سَكَتَ عَن مُّوسَى ٱلۡغَضَبُ أَخَذَ ٱلۡأَلۡوَاحَۖ وَفِي نُسۡخَتِهَا هُدٗى وَرَحۡمَةٞ لِّلَّذِينَ هُمۡ لِرَبِّهِمۡ يَرۡهَبُونَ ١٥٤\nSahl bin Abdulla said: \"Fear of Allah is the source of every good in this life and the Hereafter.\" This meaning is indicated by this verse, (And when the anger subsided in Moses, he took up the tablets; and in their inscription was guidance and mercy for those who are fearful of their Lord). Ibn Taimyah: 3/208.\nFear of Allah is the source of every good in this life and in the Hereafter. Explain in the light of this verse\nأَتُهۡلِكُنَا بِمَا فَعَلَ ٱلسُّفَهَآءُ مِنَّآۖ\nMeaning: Would You destroy us and the rest of Children of Israel for what the foolish have done -those who asked to see Allah outright and worshiped the calf- hence, Moses (u) presented his argument, disowned the foolish and pleaded with Allah not to punish them all. Ibn Juzay: 1/318.\nNeglecting to enjoin good and forbid evil is one of he biggest risks to society. Explain in the light of this verse.\nإِنۡ هِيَ إِلَّا فِتۡنَتُكَ تُضِلُّ بِهَا مَن تَشَآءُ وَتَهۡدِي مَن تَشَآءُۖ\nMeaning: It is Your trial and Your test, as You tested Your servants with prosperity and adversity, so it becomes evident who is the patient and grateful among them. Moreover, You tested them by sending Your Messengers and revealing Your Books so it becomes clear who the believer is and who is not, who the truthful is and who is not, and who the sincere is and who is not. Hence, You make that a cause for some to be guided and others to be misguided. Ibn Taimyah: 3/208.\nWhat is the wisdom behind testing with prosperity and adversity?\nwords\nأَسِفًاGrieved\nسَكَتَSubsided\nلِمِيقَاتِنَاFor Our appointment\nالرَّجفَةُPowerful earthquake"],[170,"§Al-A'raf\ndeeds\nRead a book or an article in which you learn about the attributes and characteristics of the Prophet Muhammad (ﷺ).\nRemind yourself of a Sunnah of the Prophet (ﷺ) of which you were heedless, and do it.\nTry to make it a habit, starting from today, that you enjoin good and forbid evil, even with a friend or a family member.\nguid\nFearing Allah and giving zakah and alms is a cause for receiving mercy.\nWhat Allah has made lawful for you is good and suitable for you, and that which He Has forbidden has immediate and future evil.\nWhoever seeks general and specific guidance, presently and in the future, must follow the Prophet (ﷺ) through sound evidence.\nrefl\nوَرَحۡمَتِي وَسِعَتۡ كُلَّ شَيۡءٖۚ\nAllah's mercy covered everything. Alhasan and Qatadah said: In this life, Allah's mercy encompassed the righteous and the wicked , but in the Hereafter, it is only for the righteous. Al-Baghawi: 2/157.\nWho receives Allah's mercy in this life? Who receives it in the Hereafter?\nفَسَأَكۡتُبُهَا لِلَّذِينَ يَتَّقُونَ وَيُؤۡتُونَ ٱلزَّكَوٰةَ وَٱلَّذِينَ هُم بِـَٔايَٰتِنَا يُؤۡمِنُونَ ١٥٦\nMeaning: Those who believe in all the Books and Prophets (peace be upon them); only the Muslim nation attained that. Ibn Juzay: 1/319.\nThis verse gives a glad tiding to the Muslim nation only. Why?\nوَٱلَّذِينَ هُم بِـَٔايَٰتِنَا يُؤۡمِنُونَ ١٥٦\nPart of perfect faith and belief in the revelations of Allah is to understand their meanings and act accordingly. This includes following the Prophet (ﷺ) both outwardly and inwardly, in both fundamental and minor issues of religion. Al-Saadi: 305.\nWhat are the signs of believing in the verses of Allah?\nٱلَّذِينَ يَتَّبِعُونَ ٱلرَّسُولَ ٱلنَّبِيَّ ٱلۡأُمِّيَّ ٱلَّذِي يَجِدُونَهُۥ مَكۡتُوبًا عِندَهُمۡ فِي ٱلتَّوۡرَىٰةِ وَٱلۡإِنجِيلِ\nThe illiteracy of the Prophet (ﷺ) was a functional one, where he could not write nor read out of a document, but he was the leader of all people in knowledge and recital out of memory. Ibn Taimyah: 3/210.\nWhat kind of illiteracy did the Prophet (ﷺ) have?\nوَيَضَعُ عَنۡهُمۡ إِصۡرَهُمۡ وَٱلۡأَغۡلَٰلَ ٱلَّتِي كَانَتۡ عَلَيۡهِمۡۚ\nBurden is a heavy load, where a covenant was taken upon the Children of Israel that they would perform difficult actions. With the sending of Prophet Muhammad (r), Allah has relieved them from that covenant and difficult actions, where now it is sufficient to wash the urine, permissible to take the spoils of war, and permissible to sit and eat with a menstruous woman. Al-Qurtubi: 9/356.\nDescribe the greatness of Allah's mercy upon Muslim nation where He relieved them from all burdens and heavy actions?\nفَٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ بِهِۦ وَعَزَّرُوهُ وَنَصَرُوهُ وَٱتَّبَعُواْ ٱلنُّورَ ٱلَّذِيٓ أُنزِلَ مَعَهُۥٓ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ هُمُ ٱلۡمُفۡلِحُونَ ١٥٧\n(they who have believed in him), they believed in Muhammad (ﷺ). (Honored him) revered him. (supported him) helped him against enemies. (And followed the light which was sent down with him) followed the Quran, and so they are (those who will be the successful). Al-Baghawi: 2/159.\nWhat are the traits of those who are successful that are mentioned in the book of Allah?\nوَمِن قَوۡمِ مُوسَىٰٓ أُمَّةٞ يَهۡدُونَ بِٱلۡحَقِّ وَبِهِۦ يَعۡدِلُونَ ١٥٩\nIt seems that this verse is aimed at avoiding a wrong impression that may arise from the previous verses, in which Allah had mentioned a number of the faults of the Israelites that were contrary to perfection and guidance. Some may think that this referred to all of them, therefore Allah states that among them was a group of upright people who were guided and who guided others. Al-Saadi: 306.\nThis verse comes after other verses that censured the people of Moses (u). Why?\nwords\nهُدنَاWe have turned to you in repentance\nالأُمِّيَّOne who can neither read nor write\nإِصرَهُمTheir burden\nوَعَزَّرُوهُThey honored him"],[171,"§Al-A'raf\ndeeds\nBe organized, and set a weekly schedule for your business and needs.\nReplace food items that you doubt with halal ones, as food has an impact on worship, thinking and behavior.\nRead the story of the Sabbath-breakers, and learn from it about the risk of circumventing the rules of Allah's Sharia.\nguid\nIf Allah bestows a blessing on a man or a woman, but the are not grateful to Him for it, then it will be taken away from them.\nImmorality and sins are a cause of trials that a person may not be able to endure.\nIf you are faced with adversity, remember a sin you had committed, then ask repeatedly for Allah's forgiveness.\nrefl\nوَظَلَّلۡنَا عَلَيۡهِمُ ٱلۡغَمَٰمَ وَأَنزَلۡنَا عَلَيۡهِمُ ٱلۡمَنَّ وَٱلسَّلۡوَىٰۖ كُلُواْ مِن طَيِّبَٰتِ مَا رَزَقۡنَٰكُمۡۚ وَمَا ظَلَمُونَا وَلَٰكِن كَانُوٓاْ أَنفُسَهُمۡ يَظۡلِمُونَ ١٦٠\n(They did not wrong Us) that is, when they did not give thanks to Allah or do what Allah had made obligatory for them. (But it was themselves that they wronged) that is, when they caused themselves to miss out on much good and exposed themselves to evil and divine wrath. Al-Saadi: 306.\nThis verse describes a type of self-injustice. What is it?\nفَبَدَّلَ ٱلَّذِينَ ظَلَمُواْ مِنۡهُمۡ قَوۡلًا غَيۡرَ ٱلَّذِي قِيلَ لَهُمۡ فَأَرۡسَلۡنَا عَلَيۡهِمۡ رِجۡزٗا مِّنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِ بِمَا كَانُواْ يَظۡلِمُونَ ١٦٢\nIn this verse, (The wrongdoers among them altered the words), the word (among) appeared here, however, in a similar verse in Surat Al-Baqarah, it did not. The reason it appears here is to assert that the alteration of words was not done by all of them. In Surat Al-Baqarah, the word (among) did not appear because the verse's topic is censuring and holding them all accountable for the alteration since the consequences of sins committed by the few are suffered by all. Ibn Ashur: 9/145.\nIn this verse, the word (among) appeared , however, in a similar verse in Surat Al-Baqarah, it did not. Why?\nفَبَدَّلَ ٱلَّذِينَ ظَلَمُواْ مِنۡهُمۡ قَوۡلًا غَيۡرَ ٱلَّذِي قِيلَ لَهُمۡ\nSince they changed the words, even though it was easy to abide by, then changing the ordained action is even more likely of them. Al-Saadi: 306.\nThis verse indicates the habit of wrongdoers among the Jews of defying the divine commands. Explain.\nفَبَدَّلَ ٱلَّذِينَ ظَلَمُواْ مِنۡهُمۡ قَوۡلًا غَيۡرَ ٱلَّذِي قِيلَ لَهُمۡ فَأَرۡسَلۡنَا عَلَيۡهِمۡ رِجۡزٗا مِّنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِ بِمَا كَانُواْ يَظۡلِمُونَ ١٦٢\nIf Allah bestows a blessing on a man or a woman, but they are not grateful to Him for it, then it will be taken away from them, no matter who they are, and whether they like it or not. Al-Jaza'iri: 2/252.\nIn light of this verse, what is the risk of not being grateful to Allah for His blessings?\nوَسۡـَٔلۡهُمۡ عَنِ ٱلۡقَرۡيَةِ ٱلَّتِي كَانَتۡ حَاضِرَةَ ٱلۡبَحۡرِ إِذۡ يَعۡدُونَ فِي ٱلسَّبۡتِ إِذۡ تَأۡتِيهِمۡ حِيتَانُهُمۡ يَوۡمَ سَبۡتِهِمۡ شُرَّعٗا وَيَوۡمَ لَا يَسۡبِتُونَ لَا تَأۡتِيهِمۡۚ كَذَٰلِكَ نَبۡلُوهُم بِمَا كَانُواْ يَفۡسُقُونَ ١٦٣\nThis verse contains a sharp rebuke to those who circumvent prohibited actions while claiming to be Faqih (scholars in Fiqh) when, in reality, they are not. A true scholar who fears Allah will never allow usury, a marriage of man who makes a woman lawful for her first husband. Moreover, the separation of husband and wife for compensation in order to resolve a suspended divorcee, etc. If similar abhorrent actions were taken by people against each other, it would be considered extremely repugnant, then, how about if these were taken against the commands of One Who Knows the secret and what is even more hidden. Ibn Taimyah: 3/215.\nIn light of this verse, describe the risk of circumventing the laws of Sharia?\nوَسۡـَٔلۡهُمۡ عَنِ ٱلۡقَرۡيَةِ ٱلَّتِي كَانَتۡ حَاضِرَةَ ٱلۡبَحۡرِ إِذۡ يَعۡدُونَ فِي ٱلسَّبۡتِ إِذۡ تَأۡتِيهِمۡ حِيتَانُهُمۡ يَوۡمَ سَبۡتِهِمۡ شُرَّعٗا وَيَوۡمَ لَا يَسۡبِتُونَ لَا تَأۡتِيهِمۡۚ كَذَٰلِكَ نَبۡلُوهُم بِمَا كَانُواْ يَفۡسُقُونَ ١٦٣\nAllah states that because they were defiantly disobedient, He tested them by bringing the fish on the Sabbath, and keeping them off on other days. This is similar to testing one who is on pilgrimage with easy game, and when he is not on pilgrimage, no game is around. Or, finding one who deals in usury rather than one who deals in selling. Ibn Taimyah: 3/215.\nThey were tested because they were defiantly disobedient. How?\nوَسۡـَٔلۡهُمۡ عَنِ ٱلۡقَرۡيَةِ ٱلَّتِي كَانَتۡ حَاضِرَةَ ٱلۡبَحۡرِ إِذۡ يَعۡدُونَ فِي ٱلسَّبۡتِ\nThey used to say, we are the children of Allah and His beloved because we are the descendants of His close friend Abraham and Jacob, His converser Moses and His [alleged] son Ezra . Allah says to His Prophet Muhammad (ﷺ) to ask them about the town by the sea: Have I not punished them for their sin, which was circumventing a law of Sharia. Al-Qurtubi: 9/362.\nKinship to Prophets does not prevent Allah's punishment of one who disobeyed. Explain in light of this verse.\nwords\nوَقَطَّعنَاهُمُAnd We divided them\nفَانبَجَسَتGushed forth with water\nيَعدُونَ فِي السَّبتِThey broke the Sabbath by fishing\nشُرَّعًاAppearing on the surface of the water\nلاَ يَسبِتُونَAnd when it was not Sabbath for them"],[172,"§Al-A'raf\ndeeds\nSay, \"O Allah, I seek protection in Your pleasure from Your anger, and I seek protection in Your forgiveness from Your punishment.\"\nRead a Surah from the last quarter of the Quran, and apply its ordinances.\nPerform the daily prayers in congregation.\nguid\nBeware of those who impede others from saying the truth, as they exist everywhere at all times.\nDo not forget nor dismiss the advice of one who admonishes you to remind you of Allah.\nWhether you are in prosperity or adversity, it is all a test from Allah, so be always with Him during the changes.\nrefl\nوَإِذۡ قَالَتۡ أُمَّةٞ مِّنۡهُمۡ لِمَ تَعِظُونَ قَوۡمًا ٱللَّهُ مُهۡلِكُهُمۡ أَوۡ مُعَذِّبُهُمۡ عَذَابٗا شَدِيدٗاۖ قَالُواْ مَعۡذِرَةً إِلَىٰ رَبِّكُمۡ وَلَعَلَّهُمۡ يَتَّقُونَ ١٦٤\nThe Children of Israel were divided into three groups: A group that broke the Sabbath, a second group who denounced the action of the first group and distanced themselves from them, and a third group who remained silent and distanced themselves, so they neither denounced nor broke the Sabbath. When this third group saw the persistence of the denouncers and the tyranny of the breakers, they said to the denouncers: Why do you denounce a people whom Allah will destroy or torment? They answered: We denounce them to excuse ourselves before Allah, and perhaps they may fear Allah. The Sabbath-breakers were destroyed, and the denouncers were saved, but differences arose concerning whether the third group was destroyed for their silence, or saved for distancing themselves and abstaining from sin. Ibn Juzay: 1/326.\nWhen evil is spread out in a society, people are divided into three groups; what are they? And what is the fate of each group?\nوَإِذۡ قَالَتۡ أُمَّةٞ مِّنۡهُمۡ لِمَ تَعِظُونَ قَوۡمًا ٱللَّهُ مُهۡلِكُهُمۡ أَوۡ مُعَذِّبُهُمۡ عَذَابٗا شَدِيدٗاۖ قَالُواْ مَعۡذِرَةً إِلَىٰ رَبِّكُمۡ وَلَعَلَّهُمۡ يَتَّقُونَ ١٦٤\nThe main aim behind objecting to and denouncing evil is so as to discharge one's duty and establish proof against the one to whom it is addressed, in the hope that Allah may guide him, so that he will then comply with what is enjoined or forbidden. Al-Saadi: 307.\nWhat is the main aim behind enjoining good and forbidding evil?\nفَلَمَّا نَسُواْ مَا ذُكِّرُواْ بِهِۦٓ أَنجَيۡنَا ٱلَّذِينَ يَنۡهَوۡنَ عَنِ ٱلسُّوٓءِ\nThis is the way of Allah in dealing with His servants; when the punishment comes down, He saves those who enjoined what is good and forbade what is evil. Al-Saadi: 307.\nWhat is the benefit, in this life, for those who enjoin good and forbid evil?\nإِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَسَرِيعُ ٱلۡعِقَابِ وَإِنَّهُۥ لَغَفُورٞ رَّحِيمٞ ١٦٧\nThis verse mentions both mercy and punishment, so that no despair is felt. Allah often mentions exhortation and intimidation together, so that hearts always have a sense of hope and fear. Ibn Kathir: 2/249.\nAllah mentions mercy and punishment together. Why?\nوَبَلَوۡنَٰهُم بِٱلۡحَسَنَٰتِ وَٱلسَّيِّـَٔاتِ لَعَلَّهُمۡ يَرۡجِعُونَ ١٦٨\n(And We tested them with prosperity) with good crops and health. (And adversity) with drought and hardship. (So that they would return), return to the obedience of their Lord and repent to Him. Al-Baghawi: 2/164.\nWhat is wisdom behind testing people with prosperity and adversity?\nأَلَمۡ يُؤۡخَذۡ عَلَيۡهِم مِّيثَٰقُ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ أَن لَّا يَقُولُواْ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ إِلَّا ٱلۡحَقَّ وَدَرَسُواْ مَا فِيهِۗ\n(And they had studied its teachings) so they had no problem in understanding it. But they did what they did deliberately, aware of what they were doing, and this is a greater sin and more blameworthy, and deserves a more severe punishment. Al-Saadi: 307.\nIf a sin is committed by two persons, a knowledgeable and an ignorant, what is the difference between their actions?\nوَٱلَّذِينَ يُمَسِّكُونَ بِٱلۡكِتَٰبِ وَأَقَامُواْ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ إِنَّا لَا نُضِيعُ أَجۡرَ ٱلۡمُصۡلِحِينَ ١٧٠\n(Those who hold fast), the Arabic word used for (hold fast) indicates frequent repetition in holding on to the Book of Allah and His Religion. They are praised for that since adherence to the Book of Allah and His Religion requires commitment and repetition. Al-Qurtubi: 9/374.\nThe Arabic word used for (hold fast) to the Book of Allah has a significant meaning. What is it?\nwords\nبَئِيسٍA severe torment\nعَتَواThey flagrantly defied\nخَاسِئِينَDespised\nيَسُومُهُمWho afflicts them\nعَرَضَ هَذَا الأَدنَىTaking the gains of this lower life, such as bribery\nوَدَرَسُوا مَا فِيهِThey learned the teachings of the Book, but neglected it"],[173,"§Al-A'raf\ndeeds\nSay few words in a Quran study circle, or share a message about the risk of learning knowledge or memorizing the Quran for other than the sake of Allah.\nRead the story of the man mentioned in these verses from references in Quran interpretation, and draw important lessons.\nToday, avoid anything that distracts you from the Book of Allah.\nguid\nOne of the reasons to attain piety is taking the Book (Quran) and its rulings with diligence, and studying what is in it.\nStorytelling is an effective method when calling others to Allah, and is ordained by Allah, the Almighty.\nGuidance and misguidance are in the Hand of Allah, the Almighty, so ask Him for guidance.\nrefl\nأَوۡ تَقُولُوٓاْ إِنَّمَآ أَشۡرَكَ ءَابَآؤُنَا مِن قَبۡلُ وَكُنَّا ذُرِّيَّةٗ مِّنۢ بَعۡدِهِمۡۖ أَفَتُهۡلِكُنَا بِمَا فَعَلَ ٱلۡمُبۡطِلُونَ ١٧٣\nMeaning: Allah has instilled in your natural disposition what could tell you that your forefathers followed falsehood, and that the truth is what was brought by the Messengers, and this truth should stand up to the ways you found your forefathers following and prevail over it. Yes, a person may think that the views and corrupt ways of his misguided forefathers to be true, but that is only because he is turning away from the proof and evidence of Allah and His signs in the universe and himself. So, his turning away from the truth and tending to what the falsifiers said may be the reason for him to end up on a path where he prefers falsehood to truth. Al-Saadi: 308\nWhy do some people follow the ways of their fathers and neglect what the Messengers brought?\nوَٱتۡلُ عَلَيۡهِمۡ نَبَأَ ٱلَّذِيٓ ءَاتَيۡنَٰهُ ءَايَٰتِنَا فَٱنسَلَخَ مِنۡهَا فَأَتۡبَعَهُ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنُ فَكَانَ مِنَ ٱلۡغَاوِينَ ١٧٥\nThis person shunned the attributes that are expected of one who has knowledge of the revelations of Allah, because that knowledge should make a person acquire the noblest of characteristics, do the best of deeds, and be elevated to the highest of levels and most sublime of statuses. But this man threw the Book of Allah behind his back and cast aside the manners and conduct enjoined by the Book, and took it off as he would take his clothes off. When he detached himself from it, satan caught up with him and gained power over him when he departed from that strong fortress and enticed him to sin. Thus, he became the lowest of the low (and he became of the deviators), after he had been one of those who were guided and guided others. Al-Saadi: 308.\nWhat is the risk of neglecting to follow the Book of Allah after studying and gaining its knowledge?\nوَٱتۡلُ عَلَيۡهِمۡ نَبَأَ ٱلَّذِيٓ ءَاتَيۡنَٰهُ ءَايَٰتِنَا فَٱنسَلَخَ مِنۡهَا فَأَتۡبَعَهُ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنُ فَكَانَ مِنَ ٱلۡغَاوِينَ ١٧٥\nWhen he became stubborn and did not practice what he knew, a devilish darkness came upon his heart which enabled satan to continue to use and misguide him. Detachment from the signs of Allah is a result of satan's whispers. If one follows his whispering, satan will take control of him, enslave him and continue to misguide him, which is expressed by (so satan pursued him), and so he became of those who are entrenched deviators. Ibn Ashur: 9/176.\nWhat is the risk in surrendering to the whispers of satan?\nوَٱتۡلُ عَلَيۡهِمۡ نَبَأَ ٱلَّذِيٓ ءَاتَيۡنَٰهُ ءَايَٰتِنَا فَٱنسَلَخَ مِنۡهَا فَأَتۡبَعَهُ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنُ فَكَانَ مِنَ ٱلۡغَاوِينَ ١٧٥ وَلَوۡ شِئۡنَا لَرَفَعۡنَٰهُ بِهَا وَلَٰكِنَّهُۥٓ أَخۡلَدَ إِلَى ٱلۡأَرۡضِ وَٱتَّبَعَ هَوَىٰهُۚ\nIn these verses, we find encouragement to act upon knowledge, for that raises one in status before Allah and protects him against satan. At the same time, there is a warning against not acting upon knowledge, for that will take one to the lowest of levels and will give satan power over him. This also shows us that following whims and desires and being preoccupied with such matters will lead to Allah forsaking him. Al-Saadi: 309.\nWhat is the importance of putting knowledge into practice?\nوَلَوۡ شِئۡنَا لَرَفَعۡنَٰهُ بِهَا وَلَٰكِنَّهُۥٓ أَخۡلَدَ إِلَى ٱلۡأَرۡضِ وَٱتَّبَعَ هَوَىٰهُۚ\n(And if We had willed, We could have elevated him) indicates that these signs could have been a cause for guidance and purity if Allah had willed for him to be successful and protected from satan's plot and deception, and did not detach himself from these signs. This is a lesson to the successful believers so that they realize the favor of Allah upon them. Meaning: If We had willed, he could have increased his good deeds with the signs that We had given him, and Allah would have elevated him with his knowledge. Ibn Ashur: 9/176.\nThe verses of the Quran are causes for guidance. Explain.\nفَمَثَلُهُۥ كَمَثَلِ ٱلۡكَلۡبِ إِن تَحۡمِلۡ عَلَيۡهِ يَلۡهَثۡ أَوۡ تَتۡرُكۡهُ يَلۡهَثۚ ذَّٰلِكَ مَثَلُ ٱلۡقَوۡمِ ٱلَّذِينَ كَذَّبُواْ بِـَٔايَٰتِنَاۚ\nAl-Qutaibi said: Panting is caused by either exhaustion or thirst, except for a dog, which pants in states of exhaustion, comfort and thirst. Hence, Allah uses the dog as an example for one who denied His signs, saying, if you either admonish or neglect him, he will still be misguided; like the dog, if you drive it away, it pants; and if you leave it, it pants. Al-Baghawi: 2/175.\nAnyone who is admonished but defies is compared to a dog. Why?\nمَن يَهۡدِ ٱللَّهُ فَهُوَ ٱلۡمُهۡتَدِيۖ وَمَن يُضۡلِلۡ فَأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ هُمُ ٱلۡخَٰسِرُونَ ١٧٨\nThis verse is a tribute to those who are guided, and prompts Muslims to turn to Allah for guidance and protection from the slippery ways of misguidance. Ibn Ashur: 9/180.\nThis verse indicates turning to Allah for guidance. How?\nwords\nنَتَقنَاWe raised\nظُلَّةٌA cloud\nذُرِّيَّةًYoung descendants\nفَأَتبَعَهُ الشَّيطَانُSo satan pursued him\nأَخلَدَ إِلَى الأَرضِHe clung to the [life of the] earth\nتَحمِل عَلَيهِyou drive him away"],[174,"§Al-A'raf\ndeeds\nAsk Allah for a righteous heart, and to make you enjoy your eyesight and hearing while seeking His obedience.\nSay, \"O Allah, show me the truth as true and inspire me to follow it.\"\nLearn the meanings of the Names of Allah, and invoke Him with them at times during which He is likely to answer. For instance, say, \"O Most Merciful, have mercy on me\", \"O Most Appreciative, accept my deeds.\"\nguid\nUse your body for which it is created.\nBeware of the plan of Allah in what He bestowed upon you.\nDo not be deceived by a sinner who is in good condition and appearance, as that could be a lure to him.\nrefl\nلَهُمۡ قُلُوبٞ لَّا يَفۡقَهُونَ بِهَا وَلَهُمۡ أَعۡيُنٞ لَّا يُبۡصِرُونَ بِهَا وَلَهُمۡ ءَاذَانٞ لَّا يَسۡمَعُونَ بِهَآۚ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ كَٱلۡأَنۡعَٰمِ بَلۡ هُمۡ أَضَلُّۚ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ هُمُ ٱلۡغَٰفِلُونَ ١٧٩\nMeaning: This does not negate the existence of the hearing or the sight, rather it negates their usefulness for following the religion of Allah. Ibn Juzay: 1/330.\nWhen are your hearing and sight considered useful?\nلَهُمۡ قُلُوبٞ لَّا يَفۡقَهُونَ بِهَا وَلَهُمۡ أَعۡيُنٞ لَّا يُبۡصِرُونَ بِهَا وَلَهُمۡ ءَاذَانٞ لَّا يَسۡمَعُونَ بِهَآۚ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ كَٱلۡأَنۡعَٰمِ بَلۡ هُمۡ أَضَلُّۚ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ هُمُ ٱلۡغَٰفِلُونَ ١٧٩\nSince they do not find the right way to a reward, they become like livestock, which are only concerned about eating and drinking, in fact, they are even more astray because livestock recognize what is good and what is harmful and follow their owner, but the disbelievers are the opposite of that. Al-Qurtubi: 9/390.\nWhy are some of children of Adam considered more astray than livestock?\nوَلِلَّهِ ٱلۡأَسۡمَآءُ ٱلۡحُسۡنَىٰ فَٱدۡعُوهُ بِهَاۖ\nAllah calls His names \"the best\", because they are beautiful to the ears and hearts. They point to the Oneness of Allah, His generosity, munificence, mercy and blessings. Al-Qurtubi: 9/393.\nAllah calls His names \"the best\", why?\nوَلِلَّهِ ٱلۡأَسۡمَآءُ ٱلۡحُسۡنَىٰ فَٱدۡعُوهُ بِهَاۖ\nMeaning: Ask Allah by His names, and for each request, invoke the corresponding name of Allah, such as \"O Most Merciful, have mercy on me\" and \"O the All-Wise, judge for me\". Al-Qurtubi: 9/393.\nHow does a Muslim invoke Allah's names?\nوَذَرُواْ ٱلَّذِينَ يُلۡحِدُونَ فِيٓ أَسۡمَٰٓئِهِۦۚ سَيُجۡزَوۡنَ مَا كَانُواْ يَعۡمَلُونَ ١٨٠\n(And leave those who practice deviation concerning His names) leave those who practice deviation concerning His names by abstaining from debating them, as it is clear that they do not seek to know the truth; or avoid listening to what they say, lest they deceive the rest of the believers with their doubts. Ibn Ashur: 9/189.\nWhat is meant by (leave those who practice deviation concerning His names)?\nوَمِمَّنۡ خَلَقۡنَآ أُمَّةٞ يَهۡدُونَ بِٱلۡحَقِّ وَبِهِۦ يَعۡدِلُونَ ١٨١\nThis verse indicates that Allah does not allow, in this life, the absence of those who call to the truth at all times. Al-Qurtubi: 9/397.\nHas there ever been a time when no one calls to the truth in this life?\nوَٱلَّذِينَ كَذَّبُواْ بِـَٔايَٰتِنَا سَنَسۡتَدۡرِجُهُم مِّنۡ حَيۡثُ لَا يَعۡلَمُونَ ١٨٢ وَأُمۡلِي لَهُمۡۚ إِنَّ كَيۡدِي مَتِينٌ ١٨٣\nAl-Kalbi said: \"Allah makes their actions appealing to them, then He destroys them.\" Ad-Dahhak said: \"Every time they commit a sin, We provide them with a new blessing.\" Sufyan Al-Thawri said: \"We bestow blessings upon them, and make them forget to be grateful for them.\" Al-Baghawi: 2/176.\nHow are people gradually led to destruction without them realizing it?\nwords\nذَرَأنَاWe have created\nيَعدِلُونَThey establish justice\nوَأُملِي لَهُمI will give them respite\nيَعمَهُونَWandering blindly\nأَيَّانَ مُرسَاهَاWhen will it be\nحَفِيٌّ عَنهَاWell-aware of it"],[175,"§Al-A'raf\ndeeds\nGive good tidings to those around you about the goodness in store for them with Allah; like the imminence of Allah's help, his alleviation, his Paradise and honor for those who obey Him.\nSay, \"O Allah, I seek refuge with you, lest I associate anything with you while I know, and I seek your forgiveness for what I do not know.\"\nDiscuss with some of those who seek to fulfill their needs from other than Allah, at a grave site or a shrine of a dead person, and expose the weakness of the dead to them.\nguid\nIf those in charge of shrines and grave sites were truthful, evil would not have befallen them.\nOne of the tasks of the Prophet (ﷺ) is to be a bearer of glad tidings and a warner, so make it one of your tasks in life.\nIf you receive a blessing, thank Allah before thanking others.\nrefl\nقُل لَّآ أَمۡلِكُ لِنَفۡسِي نَفۡعٗا وَلَا ضَرًّا إِلَّا مَا شَآءَ ٱللَّهُۚ\n(Say, \"I have no power to benefit) I cannot benefit myself by gaining a profit; (or harm myself) or fend off harm from myself. Al-Baghawi: 2/178.\nHow do you set right the beliefs of one who asks the Prophet (ﷺ) for help?\nإِنۡ أَنَا۠ إِلَّا نَذِيرٞ وَبَشِيرٞ لِّقَوۡمٖ يُؤۡمِنُونَ ١٨٨\nThose who believe are singled out for the glad tidings and warning because they are the ones who actually benefit from them. Ibn Juzay: 1/332.\nThose who believe are singled out for the glad tidings and warning. Why?\nفَلَمَّآ أَثۡقَلَت دَّعَوَا ٱللَّهَ رَبَّهُمَا لَئِنۡ ءَاتَيۡتَنَا صَٰلِحٗا لَّنَكُونَنَّ مِنَ ٱلشَّٰكِرِينَ ١٨٩ فَلَمَّآ ءَاتَىٰهُمَا صَٰلِحٗا جَعَلَا لَهُۥ شُرَكَآءَ فِيمَآ ءَاتَىٰهُمَاۚ\n(But when He gives them a healthy child), according to their request, and He completes the blessing upon them (they ascribed partners to Him in that which He has given them), that is, they ascribe partners to Allah with regard to that child -whom only Allah brought into being and blessed them with, thus bringing joy to his parents- by giving him a name suggesting that he is a slave (abd) of something other than Allah, such as Abdul-Harith, Abdul-Uzza, Abdul-Ka'bah, and so on, or they join others with Allah in worship, after Allah bestowed upon them blessings no one could enumerate. Al-Saadi: 311.\nState two examples of being ungrateful for the blessing of offspring?\nفَلَمَّآ أَثۡقَلَت دَّعَوَا ٱللَّهَ رَبَّهُمَا لَئِنۡ ءَاتَيۡتَنَا صَٰلِحٗا لَّنَكُونَنَّ مِنَ ٱلشَّٰكِرِينَ ١٨٩ فَلَمَّآ ءَاتَىٰهُمَا صَٰلِحٗا جَعَلَا لَهُۥ شُرَكَآءَ فِيمَآ ءَاتَىٰهُمَاۚ\nThen, Allah created the offspring in the wombs of the mothers during a specified period in which they long for the child and pray to Allah to bring him forth safe and sound. Moreover, Allah completes His blessing to them and grants them their request. Does He not deserve that they should worship Him alone and not ascribe any partner to Him in their worship, and devote their worship solely to Him? But they did the opposite, and ascribed to Him partners who (cannot create anything, but are themselves created ` They cannot help them), namely their worshippers (nor can they help themselves). Al-Saadi: 311.\nState an example of the ignorance and disbelief of the polytheists?\nأَلَهُمۡ أَرۡجُلٞ يَمۡشُونَ بِهَآۖ أَمۡ لَهُمۡ أَيۡدٖ يَبۡطِشُونَ بِهَآۖ أَمۡ لَهُمۡ أَعۡيُنٞ يُبۡصِرُونَ بِهَآۖ أَمۡ لَهُمۡ ءَاذَانٞ يَسۡمَعُونَ بِهَاۗ قُلِ ٱدۡعُواْ شُرَكَآءَكُمۡ ثُمَّ كِيدُونِ فَلَا تُنظِرُونِ ١٩٥\nThen, Allah, the Almighty, rebuked them and discredited their thinking, saying, (Do they have feet to walk with? Or hands to grasp with? Or eyes to see with? Or ears to hear with...), which means that you are actually better then these idols, so how come you are worshiping them? The aim of this verse is to expose their ignorance. Al-Qurtubi: 9/416.\nIn light of this verse, Allah favored us over the polytheists. How?\nأَلَهُمۡ أَرۡجُلٞ يَمۡشُونَ بِهَآۖ أَمۡ لَهُمۡ أَيۡدٖ يَبۡطِشُونَ بِهَآۖ أَمۡ لَهُمۡ أَعۡيُنٞ يُبۡصِرُونَ بِهَآۖ أَمۡ لَهُمۡ ءَاذَانٞ يَسۡمَعُونَ بِهَاۗ قُلِ ٱدۡعُواْ شُرَكَآءَكُمۡ ثُمَّ كِيدُونِ فَلَا تُنظِرُونِ ١٩٥\nAllah singles out for mention the feet, hands, eyes and ears because they are the tools for attaining knowledge, striving and overpowering to achieve victory. Ibn Ashur: 9/222.\nAllah singles out for mention the feet, hands, eyes and ears. Why?\nقُلِ ٱدۡعُواْ شُرَكَآءَكُمۡ ثُمَّ كِيدُونِ فَلَا تُنظِرُونِ ١٩٥\nMeaning: Call on your idols to harm me and plot against me, and do no give me anytime, as you and your idols cannot harm me. The aim of this verse is to prove the helplessness of their idols and their inability to cause harm. It also indicates the importance of relying upon Allah, holding firmly to Him, and that none other than Him is capable of all things. Ibn Juzay: 1/333.\nInvoking other than Allah and calling for their help is useless. What is the sign for realizing that?\nwords\nلِيَسكُنَTo find comfort\nتَغَشَّاهَاHe had sexual intercourse [with his wife]\nفَمَرَّت بِهِShe carried it with ease [a light pregnancy]\nأَثقَلَتWhen she grew heavy [a heavy pregnancy]\nفَتَعَالَىExalted (is Allah)"],[176,"§Al-A'raf\ndeeds\nRepeat this verse often, and say it at times of hardships and adversity.\nForgive a person who did you wrong.\nSay, \"I seek refuge with Allah from satan, the accursed,\" whenever you feel satan's whispers.\nguid\nIslam is a set of beliefs, morals and good treatments.\nThe brotherhood of human devils is a bad omen since they spare no effort in plunging their friend into sin which is evil and corruption.\nWhenever you feel discouraged from doing good, or an urge to do evil, then it is a satan's whisper, so seek refuge with Allah from that.\nrefl\nوَهُوَ يَتَوَلَّى ٱلصَّٰلِحِينَ ١٩٦\nBecause the righteous believers take their Lord as their ally, believing in Him and fearing Him, and they do not take as an ally anyone other than Him, who can do no benefit or harm. Allah protects them and helps them to do that which is good for them and in their best interests in both spiritual and worldly terms, and by virtue of their faith He wards off from them all harm. Al-Saad: 312.\nHow can one become among the allies of Allah, the Almighty?\nوَأَعۡرِضۡ عَنِ ٱلۡجَٰهِلِينَ ١٩٩\nIf one acts foolishly toward you, do not treat him with the same. Al-Baghawi: 2/184.\nIf one reviles you or acts foolishly toward you, what should you do?\nوَإِمَّا يَنزَغَنَّكَ مِنَ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنِ نَزۡغٞ فَٱسۡتَعِذۡ بِٱللَّهِۚ إِنَّهُۥ سَمِيعٌ عَلِيمٌ ٢٠٠\nThe temptation by satan is his evil whisper to cast doubts on the truth, his call to committing sins, or inducing anger, so Allah commands seeking refuge with Him when that happens. It is narrated in Hadith that in one instance, a man became very angry, and so the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \"I know a word (sentence) the saying of which will cause his anger to go away if he says it: We seek refuge with Allah from satan, the accursed.\" Ibn Juzay: 1/335.\nGive examples of temptations by satan?\nوَإِمَّا يَنزَغَنَّكَ مِنَ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنِ نَزۡغٞ فَٱسۡتَعِذۡ بِٱللَّهِۚ إِنَّهُۥ سَمِيعٌ عَلِيمٌ ٢٠٠\n(Seek refuge with Allah), ask Allah to save you from that; Allah commands to ward off satan's whispers by seeking refuge with Him. Al-Qurtubi: 9/423.\nHow does the believer ward off satan's whispers in accordance with the guidance of the Quran?\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱتَّقَوۡاْ إِذَا مَسَّهُمۡ طَٰٓئِفٞ مِّنَ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنِ تَذَكَّرُواْ فَإِذَا هُم مُّبۡصِرُونَ ٢٠١\nMeaning: They become aware of their sins by remembering and reflecting. As-Suddi said: When they commit a sin, they repent. Al-Baghawi: 2/185.\nHow does the believer react when he commits a sin?\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱتَّقَوۡاْ إِذَا مَسَّهُمۡ طَٰٓئِفٞ مِّنَ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنِ تَذَكَّرُواْ فَإِذَا هُم مُّبۡصِرُونَ ٢٠١\nSaeed ibn Jubair said: This is an example of a man who when he gets angry, he remembers Allah and restrains his anger. Laith narrated that Mujahid said: This is an example of a man who when he intends to commit a sin, he remembers Allah and refrains from it. Ibn Taimyah: 3/239.\nWho are those (when an impulse touches them from satan, they remember and at once they have insight)?\nوَٱذۡكُر رَّبَّكَ فِي نَفۡسِكَ تَضَرُّعٗا وَخِيفَةٗ وَدُونَ ٱلۡجَهۡرِ مِنَ ٱلۡقَوۡلِ بِٱلۡغُدُوِّ وَٱلۡأٓصَالِ وَلَا تَكُن مِّنَ ٱلۡغَٰفِلِينَ ٢٠٥\nThis is the etiquette to which the individual should pay proper attention, namely remembering Allah a great deal throughout the night and day, especially at the two ends of the day, sincerely, with proper focus, humility, and calmly focusing on what one says, with proper conduct and reverence, calling upon Allah and remembering Him with full presence of mind, and not being heedless, as Allah does not answer the supplication of one whose heart is heedless and not focused on what he is saying. Al-Saad: 314.\nThis verse indicates an important reason for accepting supplication and Thikr. What is it?\nwords\nخُذِ العَفوَAccept whatever little you can afford of people’s behavior, and do not burden them\nيَنزَغَنَّكَTouches you\nنَزغٌA whisper [from satan] to discourage doing good and an urge to do evil\nطَائِفٌ مِنَ الشَّيطَانِA temptation by satan\nلاَ يُقصِرُونَThey spare no effort"],[177,"§Al-Anfal\ndeeds\nSeek to reconcile between two feuding Muslims .\nRead about the reason of revelation of these verses from books on interpretation of the Quran, or from the biography of the Prophet (ﷺ).\nCheck your performance of prayer, and look for flaws in its pillars, conditions or recommended acts, then rectify these flaws.\nguid\nTrusting in Allah, and not anyone else, is an attribute of the believers.\nThe Holy Quran stresses the importance of reconciliation among people, where it is preceded by the command to fear Allah, and followed by the command to obey Allah and His Messenger while considering reconciliation as one of the conditions of faith.\nReflect on how Allah calls the fighting against His enemies \"the truth\", in contrast to those who use other distorted names for it.\nrefl\nيَسۡـَٔلُونَكَ عَنِ ٱلۡأَنفَالِۖ قُلِ ٱلۡأَنفَالُ لِلَّهِ وَٱلرَّسُولِۖ فَٱتَّقُواْ ٱللَّهَ وَأَصۡلِحُواْ ذَاتَ بَيۡنِكُمۡۖ وَأَطِيعُواْ ٱللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُۥٓ إِن كُنتُم مُّؤۡمِنِينَ ١\n(And obey Allah and His Messenger, if you are [true] believers), obey Allah and His Messenger with regard to the ruling on the spoils of war. Ubadah bin Al-Samit (may Allah be pleased with him) said: This verse was revealed about us, the Companions who fought at Badr, when we disputed among ourselves over the spoils of war, so Allah took them away from us, and made them at the disposal of His Messenger (ﷺ) who distributed them equally, and in that, we achieved the fear of Allah, the obedience of His Messenger, and reconciliation among ourselves. Ibn Juzay: 1/338.\nThis verse contains a lesson to the Muslim nation. Explain.\nإِنَّمَا ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنُونَ ٱلَّذِينَ إِذَا ذُكِرَ ٱللَّهُ وَجِلَتۡ قُلُوبُهُمۡ\nThe quality of a true believer is that when Allah is mentioned, he feels a fear in his heart, and thus implements His orders and abstains from His prohibitions. Sufyan Al-Thawri narrated that As-Suddi commented: \"A man might be thinking of committing injustice or a sin, but he abstains when he is told, \"fear Allah\", and his heart becomes fearful.\" Ibn Kathir: 2/274.\nWhat is the aim of having the hearts full of fear of Allah, the Almighty?\nوَإِذَا تُلِيَتۡ عَلَيۡهِمۡ ءَايَٰتُهُۥ زَادَتۡهُمۡ إِيمَٰنٗا\nThe reason for the increase of their faith is that they listen to it [the Quran] with presence of mind, reflecting on the meaning, and as a result of that their faith increases because reflection is one of the actions of the heart, and it is inevitable that they will learn a meaning that they did not know, or they will be reminded of something that they had forgotten, or it will make their hearts inclined toward good and make them long for the reward of their Lord, or will make them fear His punishment, or they will be deterred from sin. All of these are things that increase one's faith . Al-Saadi: 315.\nHow does reflection increases one’s faith?\nإِنَّمَا ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنُونَ ٱلَّذِينَ إِذَا ذُكِرَ ٱللَّهُ وَجِلَتۡ قُلُوبُهُمۡ وَإِذَا تُلِيَتۡ عَلَيۡهِمۡ ءَايَٰتُهُۥ زَادَتۡهُمۡ إِيمَٰنٗا وَعَلَىٰ رَبِّهِمۡ يَتَوَكَّلُونَ ٢ ٱلَّذِينَ يُقِيمُونَ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ وَمِمَّا رَزَقۡنَٰهُمۡ يُنفِقُونَ ٣\nAllah mentions the deeds of the heart [such as intentions, feelings and emotions] first, because they are the basis of physical actions and are superior to them. Al-Saadi: 315.\nAllah mentions the deeds of the heart before physical actions. Why?\nٱلَّذِينَ يُقِيمُونَ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ وَمِمَّا رَزَقۡنَٰهُمۡ يُنفِقُونَ ٣\nThe two verbs: (establish) and (spend) are in the present tense form to indicate that these are repeated and renewed actions. Ibn Ashur: 9/260.\nThe two verbs: (establish) and (spend) are in the present tense form. Why?\nإِنَّمَا ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنُونَ ٱلَّذِينَ إِذَا ذُكِرَ ٱللَّهُ وَجِلَتۡ قُلُوبُهُمۡ وَإِذَا تُلِيَتۡ عَلَيۡهِمۡ ءَايَٰتُهُۥ زَادَتۡهُمۡ إِيمَٰنٗا وَعَلَىٰ رَبِّهِمۡ يَتَوَكَّلُونَ ٢ ٱلَّذِينَ يُقِيمُونَ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ وَمِمَّا رَزَقۡنَٰهُمۡ يُنفِقُونَ ٣ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ هُمُ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنُونَ حَقّٗاۚ لَّهُمۡ دَرَجَٰتٌ عِندَ رَبِّهِمۡ وَمَغۡفِرَةٞ وَرِزۡقٞ كَرِيمٞ ٤\n(Such): Those who are described by these five qualities (are the true believers) certainly. (They will have high ranks with their Lord), they will have high standings with various heights in Paradise, and -before that- receive complete (forgiveness) of their sins. Al-Jaza’iri: 2/284.\nThe verse mentions the qualities of true believers, describe them briefly.\nوَإِذۡ يَعِدُكُمُ ٱللَّهُ إِحۡدَى ٱلطَّآئِفَتَيۡنِ أَنَّهَا لَكُمۡ وَتَوَدُّونَ أَنَّ غَيۡرَ ذَاتِ ٱلشَّوۡكَةِ تَكُونُ لَكُمۡ وَيُرِيدُ ٱللَّهُ أَن يُحِقَّ ٱلۡحَقَّ بِكَلِمَٰتِهِۦ وَيَقۡطَعَ دَابِرَ ٱلۡكَٰفِرِينَ ٧\nAllah promised the believers one of the two groups, either they would capture the caravan or defeat the army. They wanted the caravan, because Muslims were not well off and the caravan was unarmed. However, Allah wanted for them something better and more sublime than what they wanted. He wanted them to defeat the army that had come forth with the leaders and prominent figures of the polytheists. (But it was Allah’s Will to establish the truth by His Words) to support the followers of truth (and eliminate the disbelievers) means: to eradicate the people of falsehood, and to show His servants something of His support for the truth that had never crossed their minds. Al-Saadi: 316.\nWhat should be the attitude of the Muslim when Allah decrees something other than what he wants?\nwords\nالأَنفَالِSpoils of war\nوَجِلَت[Their hearts are] filled with awe\nذَاتِ الشَّوكَةِThe powerful and armed group\nدَابِرَ الكَافِرِينَ[Eliminate] all the disbelievers"],[178,"§Al-Anfal\ndeeds\nAsk Allah, persistently, to meet one of your needs because He likes to be called for help with humility.\nLook for good news about activities relating to preaching to Allah, relief and Jihad, and spread them around, as they carry glad tidings and reassurance to the believers' hearts.\nPay a visit, or send a message to someone who is engaged in charity works to strengthen and encourage him.\nguid\nStrength of the heart is more important than strength of the body, so work to strengthen your heart with faith in Allah and not to be afraid of people.\nOne of Allah's hidden soldiers is \"casting terror\" into the disbelievers' hearts, despite the power of their number and weapons.\nIf the believer embarks on a good deed to help the religion of Allah, then he must not back off or retreat.\nrefl\nوَمَا جَعَلَهُ ٱللَّهُ إِلَّا بُشۡرَىٰ وَلِتَطۡمَئِنَّ بِهِۦ قُلُوبُكُمۡۚ وَمَا ٱلنَّصۡرُ إِلَّا مِنۡ عِندِ ٱللَّهِۚ\n(Allah granted this) the sending down of the angels (only as glad tidings and to reassure your hearts) and raise your spirits; otherwise, victory is only in the Hand of Allah, not with a large number of men and weapons. Al-Saadi: 316.\nAdopting means to reach an end is a duty, but from where does true victory comes?\nوَمَا جَعَلَهُ ٱللَّهُ إِلَّا بُشۡرَىٰ وَلِتَطۡمَئِنَّ بِهِۦ قُلُوبُكُمۡۚ وَمَا ٱلنَّصۡرُ إِلَّا مِنۡ عِندِ ٱللَّهِۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ عَزِيزٌ حَكِيمٌ ١٠\nAllah pointes out that victory comes from Him -the Glorified and Sublime-, not from the angels. If it was not for Allah's victory, the number of angels would be of no avail. Al-Qurtubi: 9/458.\nThere are many reasons for achieving victory, but who is really the giver of victory?\nإِذۡ يُغَشِّيكُمُ ٱلنُّعَاسَ أَمَنَةٗ مِّنۡهُ وَيُنَزِّلُ عَلَيۡكُم مِّنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِ مَآءٗ لِّيُطَهِّرَكُم بِهِۦ وَيُذۡهِبَ عَنكُمۡ رِجۡزَ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنِ وَلِيَرۡبِطَ عَلَىٰ قُلُوبِكُمۡ وَيُثَبِّتَ بِهِ ٱلۡأَقۡدَامَ ١١\nThe (drowsiness) became an assurance to them because when they slept, the feeling of fear disappeared from their souls while they were asleep, which is a blessing. When they woke up, they felt the energy within their nerves, which gave them courage, and removed the feeling of fear which is tepidness of the nerves. Ibn Ashur: 9/278.\nHow did downness become an assurance to the believers?\nوَلِيَرۡبِطَ عَلَىٰ قُلُوبِكُمۡ\nMeaning: Make them steadfast, as steadfastness of heart leads to physical steadfastness (in battle). Al-Saadi: 316.\nAllah mentions steadfastness of the heart before physical steadfastness. Why?\nإِذۡ يُوحِي رَبُّكَ إِلَى ٱلۡمَلَٰٓئِكَةِ أَنِّي مَعَكُمۡ فَثَبِّتُواْ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْۚ\n(So strengthen those who have believed) strengthen their hearts. Al-Baghawi: 2/201.\nThis verse mentions one of the tasks of the angels. What is it?\nفَٱضۡرِبُواْ فَوۡقَ ٱلۡأَعۡنَاقِ وَٱضۡرِبُواْ مِنۡهُمۡ كُلَّ بَنَانٖ ١٢\nThe necks and fingertips are singled out for mention because striking the necks is a destruction of the disbelievers' bodies, and striking the fingertips renders the stricken unable to fight since arms are handled by fingertips. Ibn Ashur: 9/283.\nThe necks and fingertips are singled out for mention, why?\nإِذۡ يُوحِي رَبُّكَ إِلَى ٱلۡمَلَٰٓئِكَةِ أَنِّي مَعَكُمۡ فَثَبِّتُواْ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْۚ سَأُلۡقِي فِي قُلُوبِ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ ٱلرُّعۡبَ فَٱضۡرِبُواْ فَوۡقَ ٱلۡأَعۡنَاقِ وَٱضۡرِبُواْ مِنۡهُمۡ كُلَّ بَنَانٖ ١٢ ذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّهُمۡ شَآقُّواْ ٱللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُۥۚ وَمَن يُشَاقِقِ ٱللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُۥ فَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ شَدِيدُ ٱلۡعِقَابِ ١٣\nAllah cast terror into their hearts, and commanded the believers to kill them because they opposed Allah and His Messenger. Whoever opposes Allah and His Messenger, deserves such punishment. Ibn Taimyah: 3/259.\nWhat is the punishment of one who opposes Allah and His Messenger?\nwords\nيُغَشِّيكُمُHe overwhelmed you with drowsiness\nأَمَنَةًAs an assurance\nرِجزَ الشَّيطَانِsatan’s whispering and evil-suggestions\nمُتَحَرِّفًا لِقِتَالٍSwerving [as a strategy] for war\nمُتَحَيِّزًا إِلَى فِئَةٍJoining another group"],[179,"§Al-Anfal\ndeeds\nThink of an act of worship that is ordained by the Messenger (ﷺ), which you fell short in, or that you were ignorant of, and hasten to do it.\nIn prostration, say this supplication often, \"O changer of the hearts, make my heart firm on your religion,\" as the Messenger (ﷺ) used to do, for Allah comes between a person and his heart.\nDenounce what is wrong as much as you can, and beware of remaining silent, as the punishment will befall you along with the disobedient.\nguid\nIf a calamity befalls you because of one of your sins, then be aware that your recurrence to sin means that calamities will return to you again.\nBeware of turning away from the commands and prohibitions, as this may lead to many evils, the first of which is a seal on the heart.\nPostponing repentance may lead to being deprived of it, Allah forbids.\nrefl\nفَلَمۡ تَقۡتُلُوهُمۡ وَلَٰكِنَّ ٱللَّهَ قَتَلَهُمۡۚ\nMeaning: It is not because of your power and strength that you killed the pagans, who were many while you were few. Rather, it is Allah Who gave you victory over them. Ibn Kathir: 2/283.\nWho should really be accredited with killing and defeating the disbelievers?\nإِن تَسۡتَفۡتِحُواْ فَقَدۡ جَآءَكُمُ ٱلۡفَتۡحُۖ وَإِن تَنتَهُواْ فَهُوَ خَيۡرٞ لَّكُمۡۖ وَإِن تَعُودُواْ نَعُدۡ وَلَن تُغۡنِيَ عَنكُمۡ فِئَتُكُمۡ\n(If you ask for a judgement, now has the judgement come unto you), this is in reference to Abu Jahl, (the leader of the polytheists army) on the day of battle of Badr, when the two armies faced each other, he said: \"O Allah, whichever of the two parties severed ties of kinship, and brought us what we do not know, destroy him at once today.\" Al-Baghawi: 2/206.\nAllah is Forbearing with His servant until the servant brings about his own demise. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَلَن تُغۡنِيَ عَنكُمۡ فِئَتُكُمۡ شَيۡـٔٗا وَلَوۡ كَثُرَتۡ وَأَنَّ ٱللَّهَ مَعَ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ ١٩\nWhat is meant by Allah being with them is that He supports the believers to a degree commensurate with their level of faith and righteous deeds. If the enemy is given the upper hand over the believers on some occasions, that is only because of shortcomings on the believers' part and their failure to do the duties required by faith. Otherwise, if they do what Allah has enjoined in every respect, no army of theirs would ever be defeated as a final outcome, and their enemy would never have the upper hand over them in such a way that they can never recover from it. Al-Saadi: 317-318.\nHow do we reconcile Allah's care of the believers and the occasional prevail of disbelievers over them?\nإِنَّ شَرَّ ٱلدَّوَآبِّ عِندَ ٱللَّهِ ٱلصُّمُّ ٱلۡبُكۡمُ ٱلَّذِينَ لَا يَعۡقِلُونَ ٢٢\nThe hearing which Allah says they do not have is hearing in the sense of what has a positive impact on the heart. As for hearing in the sense of what establishes proof against them, Allah has established proof against them by means of what they heard of His revelations, but He did not cause them to hear in any beneficial way, because He does not see any good in them that would qualify them to listen and benefit from His revelations. Al-Saadi: 318.\nWhat is the hearing that Allah says the polytheists do not have? What do you learn from that?\nوَلَوۡ عَلِمَ ٱللَّهُ فِيهِمۡ خَيۡرٗا لَّأَسۡمَعَهُمۡۖ وَلَوۡ أَسۡمَعَهُمۡ لَتَوَلَّواْ وَّهُم مُّعۡرِضُونَ ٢٣\nThis verse indicates that not everyone who hears and understands has good in him. Rather, he may understand but does not practice, and so he becomes useless without any good in him. Also, this verse indicates that making someone hear in order to comprehend is sought for one who has good in him, as he would benefit from it. Ibn Taimyah: 3/265.\nDoes everyone who hears and understands have good in him?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ ٱسۡتَجِيبُواْ لِلَّهِ وَلِلرَّسُولِ إِذَا دَعَاكُمۡ لِمَا يُحۡيِيكُمۡۖ\nThe heart is brought to life by becoming submissive to Allah, the Almighty, consistently obeying Him and His Messenger (ﷺ). Al-Saadi: 318.\nHow can the heart be brought to life?\nوَٱعۡلَمُوٓاْ أَنَّ ٱللَّهَ يَحُولُ بَيۡنَ ٱلۡمَرۡءِ وَقَلۡبِهِۦ\nAllah comes in between a person and his heart, so he will neither believe nor disbelieve except by Allah's leave. Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \"The Prophet (ﷺ) used to say these words often, (O Changer of the hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion). We said: \"O Allah's Messenger! We believed in you and in what you brought us; are you afraid for us?\" He said: (Yes, for the hearts are between two of Allah's Fingers, He changes them (as He wills).\" Ibn Kathir: 2/285.\nKnowing that your heart is in the Hand of Allah, not yours, then what must you do?\nwords\nوَلِيُبلِيَ المُؤمِنِينَAllah tests the believers [so He may reward them and make them victorious]\nمُوهِنُAllah Weakens [the plot of the disbelievers]\nتَستَفتِحُواYou [the disbelievers] ask for Allah's judgement against the wrongdoers"],[180,"§Al-Anfal\ndeeds\nRemind your family and children, constantly, to perform their prayers on time so you would not be among those who are deluded by their wealth and children.\nAfter reading the interpretation of this verse, give a talk or share a message about the benefits of righteousness in this life and the Hereafter.\nAsk for Allah's forgiveness often, and set up a time period for yourself daily for reading Athkar (remembrance of Allah) while reminding yourself that seeking forgiveness is a cause for relieving distress and averting punishment.\nguid\nThe criterion which enables the believer to see through ambiguous matters is a light within his heart, and it is obtained through righteousness and opposing one's whim.\nThe fact that the people of truth are few in number does not necessitate their defeat.\nThe frequent seeking of Allah's forgiveness by more people is a reason to ward off punishment.\nrefl\nوَٱعۡلَمُوٓاْ أَنَّمَآ أَمۡوَٰلُكُمۡ وَأَوۡلَٰدُكُمۡ فِتۡنَةٞ\nMeaning: A test from Allah to you where He grants you so these blessings so that it becomes evident who among you will be grateful and obedient to Him, and who will be distracted and dedicated to them instead. Ibn Kathir: 2/288.\nWhen do properties and children become a blessing? When do they become an ordeal?\nوَٱعۡلَمُوٓاْ أَنَّمَآ أَمۡوَٰلُكُمۡ وَأَوۡلَٰدُكُمۡ فِتۡنَةٞ وَأَنَّ ٱللَّهَ عِندَهُۥٓ أَجۡرٌ عَظِيمٞ ٢٨\nMeaning: If you have reason and sound thinking, then you should give precedence to His great reward over small, transient, diminishing pleasure. The wise person weighs things up and gives precedence to what is more deserving of being given precedence. Al-Saadi: 319.\nThis verse provides a basis for reconciliation between the adornments of this world and the bliss of the Hereafter. Explain in the light of this verse.\nوَٱعۡلَمُوٓاْ أَنَّمَآ أَمۡوَٰلُكُمۡ وَأَوۡلَٰدُكُمۡ فِتۡنَةٞ وَأَنَّ ٱللَّهَ عِندَهُۥٓ أَجۡرٌ عَظِيمٞ ٢٨\nThis is a warning against betrayal to which the love of wealth lead, such as taking illegally part of the spoils of war, etc. Here, properties are mentioned first since they are the more likely reason for betrayal in this case. Ibn Ashur: 9/324.\nIn this verse, properties precede children in mention. Why ?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓاْ إِن تَتَّقُواْ ٱللَّهَ يَجۡعَل لَّكُمۡ فُرۡقَانٗا\nCertainly, those who have fear Allah by following what He ordains and abstaining from what He forbids, will be guided to differentiate between truth and falsehood. Ibn Kathir: 2/289.\nDistinguishing between truth and falsehood requires a criterion, how can we attain it?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓاْ إِن تَتَّقُواْ ٱللَّهَ يَجۡعَل لَّكُمۡ فُرۡقَانٗا وَيُكَفِّرۡ عَنكُمۡ سَيِّـَٔاتِكُمۡ وَيَغۡفِرۡ لَكُمۡۗ وَٱللَّهُ ذُو ٱلۡفَضۡلِ ٱلۡعَظِيمِ ٢٩\n(If you fear Allah, He will grant you a criterion), it means that Allah will make for him a way out from skepticism about the religion. 'Ikrimah (a student of Ibn Abbas) said: \"A deliverance from all fears.\" Ibn Ishaq said: \"A differentiation between truth and falsehood.\" Al-Baghawi: 2/214.\nWhat is meant by (criterion)? How can one attain it?\nوَمَا كَانَ ٱللَّهُ لِيُعَذِّبَهُمۡ وَأَنتَ فِيهِمۡۚ وَمَا كَانَ ٱللَّهُ مُعَذِّبَهُمۡ وَهُمۡ يَسۡتَغۡفِرُونَ ٣٣\n(Nor would Allah punish them while they seek forgiveness), Allah would not punish them if they believe and seek forgiveness, as seeking forgiveness is a shield against punishment. One of the righteous predecessors said: \"We used to have two shields against punishment, which are: Presence of the Prophet (ﷺ), and seeking forgiveness. After the Prophet (ﷺ) passed away, the first shield is gone while the other one still remains.\" Ibn Juzay: 1/343.\nIn light of this verse, explain the importance of seeking forgiveness.\nوَمَا كَانَ ٱللَّهُ مُعَذِّبَهُمۡ وَهُمۡ يَسۡتَغۡفِرُونَ ٣٣\nAllah makes clear that He does not punish one who is seeking His forgiveness because asking for Allah's forgiveness wipes out the sin which is the cause for punishment, and so the punishment is warded off. Ibn Taimyah: 3/268.\nAllah does not punish one who is seeking His forgiveness. Why?\nwords\nيَتَخَطَّفَكُمُ[The disbelievers] snatch you away\nفَآوَاكُمAllah sheltered you [in Al-Madinah]\nلِيُثبِتُوكَ[The disbelievers plot] to imprison you\nأَسَاطِيرُLies, ancient fables"],[181,"§Al-Anfal\ndeeds\nDonate to a charitable organization for the sake of Allah, in contrast to the actions of polytheists.\nHasten today to sincerely repent to Allah, as He has promised the disbelievers, who are more sinful than you, to accept their repentance and forgive them if they desist from their disbelief.\nShare a message in which you give glad tiding to the transgressors who commit major sins, that Allah has promised the disbelievers, who are more sinful than them, to accept their repentance and forgive them if they desist from their disbelief.\nguid\nDo not be deceived by the large number of projects and funds that are allocated to turn people away from the path of Allah, for it will be a source of regret with an evil consequence for them in this life and the Hereafter, and their plans will fail.\nThe greatest persecution is the occurrence of polytheism and its steadiness in a country; and for that Allah, the Almighty, commands to ward off this persecution, even by fighting.\nIf you know that Allah is your Protector, why should you be afraid?!\nrefl\nوَمَا لَهُمۡ أَلَّا يُعَذِّبَهُمُ ٱللَّهُ وَهُمۡ يَصُدُّونَ عَنِ ٱلۡمَسۡجِدِ ٱلۡحَرَامِ وَمَا كَانُوٓاْ أَوۡلِيَآءَهُۥٓۚ إِنۡ أَوۡلِيَآؤُهُۥٓ إِلَّا ٱلۡمُتَّقُونَ وَلَٰكِنَّ أَكۡثَرَهُمۡ لَا يَعۡلَمُونَ ٣٤\nAlhasan said: The polytheists used to say, \"We are the guardians of the Sacred Mosque,\" so Allah replied to them saying: (They are not its rightful guardians) guardians of the House of Allah (Al-Ka'bah). (Its rightful guardians are) there are no guardians except (those who fear Allah) the believers who avoid shirk. Al-Baghawi: 2/219.\nWhat is the criterion on which the rightful guardianship of the House of Allah is based?\nوَمَا كَانَ صَلَاتُهُمۡ عِندَ ٱلۡبَيۡتِ إِلَّا مُكَآءٗ وَتَصۡدِيَةٗۚ فَذُوقُواْ ٱلۡعَذَابَ بِمَا كُنتُمۡ تَكۡفُرُونَ ٣٥\nMeaning: The taking of handclapping, singing, beating tambourines, and blowing into flutes in gatherings as religious acts that get one closer to Allah, is not part of Islam, nor it was ordained by their Prophet (ﷺ) or any of his Caliphs after him. No Muslim Imam or a scholar had approved that. In fact, this was never done by any religious people since the times of the Prophet (ﷺ), his Companions, their followers and students. Al-Qasimi: 5/289.\nThe taking of handclapping, singing, and beating tambourines are considered innovations in religion. Why?\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ يُنفِقُونَ أَمۡوَٰلَهُمۡ لِيَصُدُّواْ عَن سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِۚ فَسَيُنفِقُونَهَا ثُمَّ تَكُونُ عَلَيۡهِمۡ حَسۡرَةٗ ثُمَّ يُغۡلَبُونَۗ وَٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوٓاْ إِلَىٰ جَهَنَّمَ يُحۡشَرُونَ ٣٦\nMeaning: To suppress the truth and support falsehood, resist affirmation of the Oneness of the Most Merciful, and establish the religion of idol worshipers. (They will continue to spend it), that is, they will pay all these expenses, and they would not mind, because they adhere firmly to falsehood and they strongly resent the truth. But, that will be (a source of regret for them) a cause of sorrow, disgrace and humiliation. (Then they will be defeated): They will lose their wealth and all that they hoped for, and they will be punished most severely in the Hereafter. Al-Saadi: 320.\nThe plots of the disbelievers and hypocrites and their spending to promote falsehood are strong, but what will be its outcome?\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ يُنفِقُونَ أَمۡوَٰلَهُمۡ لِيَصُدُّواْ عَن سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِۚ فَسَيُنفِقُونَهَا ثُمَّ تَكُونُ عَلَيۡهِمۡ حَسۡرَةٗ ثُمَّ يُغۡلَبُونَۗ وَٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوٓاْ إِلَىٰ جَهَنَّمَ يُحۡشَرُونَ ٣٦\nRegret is associated with wealth because spending wealth is a reason for regret. Ibn Ashur: 9/341.\nWhy is regret associated with wealth in this verse?\nقُل لِّلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوٓاْ إِن يَنتَهُواْ يُغۡفَرۡ لَهُم مَّا قَدۡ سَلَفَ وَإِن يَعُودُواْ فَقَدۡ مَضَتۡ سُنَّتُ ٱلۡأَوَّلِينَ ٣٨\nMeaning: If the disbelievers desist from what they were forbidden, their past sins will be forgiven. Ibn Taimyah: 3/474.\nAllah likes for His servant to repent. Explain in the light of this verse.\nوَقَٰتِلُوهُمۡ حَتَّىٰ لَا تَكُونَ فِتۡنَةٞ وَيَكُونَ ٱلدِّينُ كُلُّهُۥ لِلَّهِۚ\nThis is the goal of fighting and Jihad against the enemies of the faith, to ward off their evil from the faith, to defend the religion of Allah, Who created people and to follow this path so that it will be supreme over all other religions. Al-Saadi: 321.\nWhat should be the right intention and great objective of one who goes for Jihad in the cause of Allah?\nوَإِن تَوَلَّوۡاْ فَٱعۡلَمُوٓاْ أَنَّ ٱللَّهَ مَوۡلَىٰكُمۡۚ نِعۡمَ ٱلۡمَوۡلَىٰ وَنِعۡمَ ٱلنَّصِيرُ ٤٠\nThe one whose protector and helper is Allah will have no fear, but the one whom Allah opposes will have no honor and will not be able to achieve anything. Al-Saadi: 321.\nWhat does the believer benefit from knowing that Allah is his protector and helper?\nwords\nمُكَاءًWhistling\nوَتَصدِيَةًHandclapping\nفَيَركُمَهُPile up the wicked, some of them upon others\nسُنَّةُ الأَوَّلِينَOur way of punishing them if they disbelieve"],[182,"§Al-Anfal\ndeeds\nGive charity, today, to a relative, an orphan, a needy person or a stranded traveler.\nAfter reflecting on the events of battle of Badr, draw three lessons from it.\nShare a message in which you explain that Allah loves to be remembered so much that He commands doing so during the busiest of all times.\nguid\nIf you see a dream, have it interpreted only by someone who is good at that, and be optimistic.\nWhen Allah decrees something, He would set up causes that lead to it.\nThe remembrance of Allah strengthen the fighters against their enemies; would it not be enough to strengthen you to satisfy your needs and solve your problems? So, do not be heedless of it.\nrefl\nوَٱعۡلَمُوٓاْ أَنَّمَا غَنِمۡتُم مِّن شَيۡءٖ فَأَنَّ لِلَّهِ خُمُسَهُۥ وَلِلرَّسُولِ وَلِذِي ٱلۡقُرۡبَىٰ وَٱلۡيَتَٰمَىٰ وَٱلۡمَسَٰكِينِ وَٱبۡنِ ٱلسَّبِيلِ\nAssigning these spoils to the Messenger (ﷺ) because he divides these bounties as commanded by Allah, and no one has sole ownership of it. The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \"By Allah, I do not give nor withhold, for I am only a distributor who gives as directed.\" This shows that he was not the owner of these bounties, rather he managed them as directed by Allah. Ibn Taimyah: 3/278.\nWhy were the bounties of war assigned to the Messenger (ﷺ)?\nوَمَآ أَنزَلۡنَا عَلَىٰ عَبۡدِنَا يَوۡمَ ٱلۡفُرۡقَانِ يَوۡمَ ٱلۡتَقَى ٱلۡجَمۡعَانِۗ\nMeaning: It is the day of Badr, on which Allah separated truth from falsehood. Al-Qurtubi: 10/35.\nAllah calls the day of Badr: (the day of Criterion), why?\nإِذۡ أَنتُم بِٱلۡعُدۡوَةِ ٱلدُّنۡيَا وَهُم بِٱلۡعُدۡوَةِ ٱلۡقُصۡوَىٰ وَٱلرَّكۡبُ أَسۡفَلَ مِنكُمۡۚ\nThe mention of the locations of the two armies was to remind the Muslims of the critical situation in which they were at before the battle, and to draw their attention to Allah's great kindness toward them when they, unexpectedly, faced the disbelievers' army which had strength in men and arms with a good location. That was the aim of describing the locations, and if it was not for that, no details would have been provided since describing locations is not the style of the Quran, unless there is a lesson to be learned. Ibn Ashur: 10/15-16.\nWhat is the aim of describing the locations of the armies of Muslims and disbelievers in the battle of Badr?\nوَلَوۡ تَوَاعَدتُّمۡ لَٱخۡتَلَفۡتُمۡ فِي ٱلۡمِيعَٰدِ وَلَٰكِن لِّيَقۡضِيَ ٱللَّهُ أَمۡرٗا كَانَ مَفۡعُولٗا لِّيَهۡلِكَ مَنۡ هَلَكَ عَنۢ بَيِّنَةٖ وَيَحۡيَىٰ مَنۡ حَيَّ عَنۢ بَيِّنَةٖۗ\n(If you had made an appointment [to meet], you would have missed the appointment), meaning: If you had made an appointment with Quraish, then you came to know their great number versus your small number, you would have disputed among yourselves and would not meet them. Or, if you made an appointment, your meeting would not have occurred as it did with Allah's ease and kindness. (That those who perished [through disbelief] would perish upon evidence) that is, whoever dies in battle, he would do so after seeing a clear evidence of the truth; also, whoever survives, would see the same evidence. Ibn Juzay: 1/354.\nWhen Allah decrees something, He would set up causes that lead to it. Explain, in the light of this verse.\nإِذۡ يُرِيكَهُمُ ٱللَّهُ فِي مَنَامِكَ قَلِيلٗاۖ وَلَوۡ أَرَىٰكَهُمۡ كَثِيرٗا لَّفَشِلۡتُمۡ وَلَتَنَٰزَعۡتُمۡ فِي ٱلۡأَمۡرِ\nAllah had shown the polytheists to His Messenger (ﷺ) in a dream as few in number, so he told his Companions of these glad tidings, which reassured them and put them at ease. If He had shown them to you as many, and you had told your Companions about that , then (you [believers] would have lost courage and disputed in the matter). Some of you would have thought that you should go ahead and fight them, and others would have thought otherwise, so there would have been a dispute which would have led to losing heart. Al-Saadi: 322.\nHow did the dream of the Prophet (ﷺ) become reassuring for his Companions?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓاْ إِذَا لَقِيتُمۡ فِئَةٗ فَٱثۡبُتُواْ وَٱذۡكُرُواْ ٱللَّهَ كَثِيرٗا لَّعَلَّكُمۡ تُفۡلِحُونَ ٤٥\nPatience, steadfastness and remembering Allah much are among the greatest means of attaining victory. Al-Saadi: 322.\nThis verse contains the biggest causes of victory. What are they?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓاْ إِذَا لَقِيتُمۡ فِئَةٗ فَٱثۡبُتُواْ وَٱذۡكُرُواْ ٱللَّهَ كَثِيرٗا\nQatadah commented on this verse, saying: Allah commands the believers to remember Him during the busiest of all times; when clashing with the enemy by swords. Ibn Kathir: 2/302.\nHow do we infer the importance of remembrance of Allah from this verse?\nwords\nالجَمعَانِThe Muslim army and the disbelievers army\nبِالعُدوَةِ الدُّنيَاOn the side of the valley nearer to Al-Madina\nبِالعُدوَةِ القُصوَىOn the farther side\nوَالرَّكبُQuraish trade caravan\nأَسفَلَ مِنكُمCloser to the coast of the Red sea"],[183,"§Al-Anfal\ndeeds\nThrough a message or a short talk, warn those around you from the harms of disputing since it is the beginning of losing courage.\nReconcile between two feuding persons around you.\nThis verse contains two deadly sicknesses of the heart. Identify them and seek refuge with Allah from them.\nguid\nDo your utmost to unify the hearts of Muslims around Islamic Sharia, especially during the times of hardships and adversities.\nAlways, weigh your views against the Quran and Sunnah, and do not hesitate to discard any view that contradicts them, lest the devil makes it appealing to you.\nAll devils, whether jinn or humans, will abandon those whom they misguided and disown them when the punishment comes, so never give in to them.\nrefl\nوَأَطِيعُواْ ٱللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُۥ وَلَا تَنَٰزَعُواْ فَتَفۡشَلُواْ وَتَذۡهَبَ رِيحُكُمۡۖ وَٱصۡبِرُوٓاْۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ مَعَ ٱلصَّٰبِرِينَ ٤٦\nDisputing is prohibited, and the causes to avoid disputing are achieved through understanding, consulting and conferring with each other until unanimity is reached. If they dispute over something, then they should refer it to those in authority among them. Allah says, (If they referred it to the Messenger or to those in authority among them) [4:83], and (If you disagree over anything, refer it to Allah and the Messenger) [4:59]. Forbidding dispute is more general than enjoining obedience to those in authority because if they are prohibited from disputing among themselves, then disputing with those in authority is even more prohibited. Ibn Ashur: 10/30.\nList some causes to avoid disputing.\nوَأَطِيعُواْ ٱللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُۥ وَلَا تَنَٰزَعُواْ فَتَفۡشَلُواْ وَتَذۡهَبَ رِيحُكُمۡۖ وَٱصۡبِرُوٓاْۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ مَعَ ٱلصَّٰبِرِينَ ٤٦\nDisputing leads to losing courage because it stirs anger, eliminates cooperation among people, and makes some await for others' turns of misfortune. This, in turn, leads them to guard against each other, and not to expect each other's support during the hardships of fighting. Therefore, Muslim community becomes turned away from engaging in an endeavor that is beneficial to all, and the army is drawn away from marching toward the enemy, thus becomes defeated by it. Ibn Ashur: 10/30.\nList three harmful consequences of disputing.\nوَلَا تَكُونُواْ كَٱلَّذِينَ خَرَجُواْ مِن دِيَٰرِهِم بَطَرٗا وَرِئَآءَ ٱلنَّاسِ وَيَصُدُّونَ عَن سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِۚ\nMeaning: Your aim should be to seek Allah's pleasure and to make the religion of Allah supreme, to bar people from following the paths that lead to incurring the wrath and punishment of Allah and to attract people to the straight path of Allah that leads to paradise. Al-Saadi: 323.\nExplain the difference between going forth in the cause of Allah, and going forth to avert people from the way of Allah.\nوَلَا تَكُونُواْ كَٱلَّذِينَ خَرَجُواْ مِن دِيَٰرِهِم بَطَرٗا وَرِئَآءَ ٱلنَّاسِ وَيَصُدُّونَ عَن سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِۚ وَٱللَّهُ بِمَا يَعۡمَلُونَ مُحِيطٞ ٤٧\nIn Arabic language, insolence is utilizing the blessings and strength which are bestowed by Allah to disobey Him. Al-Qurtubi: 10/42.\nAllah forbids insolence, what is it?\nإِنِّيٓ أَخَافُ ٱللَّهَۚ وَٱللَّهُ شَدِيدُ ٱلۡعِقَابِ ٤٨\nAllah mentions that satan fears Him; however, punishment is deserved for neglecting a command or committing a sin. Ibn Taimyah: 3/218.\nFearing Allah is not sufficient to ward off punishment, until it is combined by adherence to His commands and abstinence from His prohibitions. Explain.\nوَمَن يَتَوَكَّلۡ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ فَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ عَزِيزٌ حَكِيمٞ ٤٩\n(Whoever relies upon Allah), whoever submits himself to Allah, and puts his trust in Him, (then indeed, Allah is Exalted in Might and Wise) Allah is the Almighty who does with His enemies whatever He wills. Al-Baghawi: 2/231.\nWhat is the pleasing outcome for someone who relies on Allah and entrusts all matters to Him?\nوَلَوۡ تَرَىٰٓ إِذۡ يَتَوَفَّى ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ ٱلۡمَلَٰٓئِكَةُ يَضۡرِبُونَ وُجُوهَهُمۡ وَأَدۡبَٰرَهُمۡ وَذُوقُواْ عَذَابَ ٱلۡحَرِيقِ ٥٠\nThis occurs at the time of the disbelievers death; the angels strike their faces and backs with whips of fire. Al-Baghawi: 2/231.\nThe disbelievers are punished at the time of their death. How?\nwords\nبَطَرًاInsolently\nجَارٌ لَكُمYour protector and helper\nتَرَاءَتِFaced each other\nنَكَصَHe turned back\nكَدَأبِLike the custom, habitual ways"],[184,"§Al-Anfal\ndeeds\nSearch within yourself for a sin of which you are heedless and repent from it, so that Allah may change you for the better.\nReflect upon the story of Pharaoh and his demise, then draw three lessons from it.\nSearch within yourself for a skill that Allah has bestowed upon you, then use it in His obedience and serving His religion.\nguid\nThe basis of a happy life is repentance and frequent worship.\nIf you make a promise, then never break it or breach a covenant, even if it is with the disbelievers, for that is not a trait of the believers.\nIn contrast to what is projected in the media, deterring the enemies of Islam is ordained by Sharia, whether it is presenting evidence through debate and argument, or organizing materials and soldiers for war, which is similar to what they do to us.\nrefl\nذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَمۡ يَكُ مُغَيِّرٗا نِّعۡمَةً أَنۡعَمَهَا عَلَىٰ قَوۡمٍ حَتَّىٰ يُغَيِّرُواْ مَا بِأَنفُسِهِمۡ\nMeaning: Allah, the Almighty, will never change His blessings upon a people until they change what is within themselves into denial and ingratitude. Once they do that, Allah will change their situation and take away His blessings. Al-Baghawi: 2/232.\nWhen does Allah change the condition of a society?\nذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَمۡ يَكُ مُغَيِّرٗا نِّعۡمَةً أَنۡعَمَهَا عَلَىٰ قَوۡمٍ حَتَّىٰ يُغَيِّرُواْ مَا بِأَنفُسِهِمۡ\n(That), is namely the punishment that Allah sent upon the disbelieving nations, and took away from them what they were enjoying of blessings and a life of ease, was because of their sins and the change in their own attitude and conduct. For verily Allah would not change a favor which He had bestowed upon a people, whether those blessings are spiritual or worldly; rather, He would preserve and increases those blessings for them, if they increase in gratitude toward Him (until they change what is within themselves), turning from obedience to disobedience. Thus, showing ingratitude for the blessings of Allah, and using them for sinful purposes; and in that case, Allah takes the blessings away from them, and changes them into something else as they changed their attitude and conduct. Allah is wise in doing that, and He is just and kind to His servants, as He does not punish them except for their wrongdoing. Al-Saadi: 324.\nWhen one changes what is within himself, his blessing will be taken away, so, what about one who is steadfast in gratitude towards Allah?\nذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَمۡ يَكُ مُغَيِّرٗا نِّعۡمَةً أَنۡعَمَهَا عَلَىٰ قَوۡمٍ حَتَّىٰ يُغَيِّرُواْ مَا بِأَنفُسِهِمۡ\nThis change consists of two types. First: They display the change through words and actions, and hence, this entails censure and punishment. Second: They replace the faith within their hearts with doubt, suspicion and hatred, and intend to disobey Allah and His Messenger (ﷺ). Ibn Taimyah: 3/282.\nThere are two types of change to oneself, outward and inward. Explain.\nٱلَّذِينَ عَٰهَدتَّ مِنۡهُمۡ ثُمَّ يَنقُضُونَ عَهۡدَهُمۡ فِي كُلِّ مَرَّةٖ وَهُمۡ لَا يَتَّقُونَ ٥٦\nIn the Arabic text, the verb (break) is in the present tense form to indicate that their action reoccurs and is often repeated even after the revelation of this verse. They will not desist from it, so this alludes to the fact that keeping their covenant is hopeless. Ibn Ashur: 10/48.\nThe verb (break) is in the present tense. Why?\nفَإِمَّا تَثۡقَفَنَّهُمۡ فِي ٱلۡحَرۡبِ فَشَرِّدۡ بِهِم مَّنۡ خَلۡفَهُمۡ لَعَلَّهُمۡ يَذَّكَّرُونَ ٥٧\nThese are the benefits of the punishments and prescribed penalties for sins; they are a means of deterring those who have not committed sins, and they also deter those who committed them from repeating them. Al-Saadi: 324.\nWhat are the benefits of punishing the sinners?\nوَإِمَّا تَخَافَنَّ مِن قَوۡمٍ خِيَانَةٗ فَٱنۢبِذۡ إِلَيۡهِمۡ عَلَىٰ سَوَآءٍۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَا يُحِبُّ ٱلۡخَآئِنِينَ ٥٨\nThis verse hangs throwing back the treaty on the fear of betrayal, not its occurrence, because political and war-related affairs are based on suspicions and changing situations. If those in authority wait for a suspected matter to occur, it will subject Muslim society to danger or embroilment in heedlessness and a loss of benefit. Ibn Ashur: 10/52.\nThe verse hangs throwing back the treaty on the fear of betrayal, not its occurrence. Why?\nوَإِن جَنَحُواْ لِلسَّلۡمِ فَٱجۡنَحۡ لَهَا\nFor in that there are many benefits, such as; first: Seeking peace and safety is always good if they are the ones who initiate that, then it is more appropriate to respond. Second: It offers an opportunity to regain your strength and prepare again to fight them at some other time, if necessary. Third: If you make peace with one another, feel safe with one another, and each side starts to know the beliefs of the other, as Islam by its nature will prevail and cannot be prevailed over. Whoever is possessed of reason and understanding, if he is fair-minded, will inevitably choose Islam over other religions. Al-Saadi: 325.\nWhat are the benefits of making peace for Muslims, when it is offered by the disbelievers and all of its conditions were met?\nwords\nتَثقَفَنَّهُمYou find them\nفَانبِذThrow their treaty back to them\nعَلَى سَوَاءٍ[Putting you] on equal terms\nجَنَحُواThey inclined\nفَاجنَحYou incline"]])